    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20361": {
      "title": "POSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PARTIEL EN ANATOMIE HUMAINE (CORRESPONDANT A 0,05 ETP AU FORFAIT HORAIRE DE 15 H/AN)",
      "description": " \n  \n \n  \nSOUS RESERVE DE L’APPROBATION DU CONSEIL ACADEMIQUE DU 23 NOVEMBRE 2026 \n  \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PARTIEL EN ANATOMIE HUMAINE \n(CORRESPONDANT A 0,05 ETP AU FORFAIT HORAIRE DE 15 H/AN) \nFACULTE DES SCIENCES \n \n \nRéférence : 2027/A018 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures :  04/01/2027 à midi  \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 01/10/2027 \nDescriptif du poste \nLa Faculté des Sciences ouvre un poste Académique temps partiel de 0. 05 ETP dans le cadre d’un \nbachelier en Sciences biologiques organisé conjointement par l'Université de Mons (UMons) et \nl'Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB) sur le campus de Charleroi Ville Haute. Il s’agit d’assurer \nl’enseignement d’un cours d’Anatomie humaine dispensé aux étudiants de la première et deuxième \nannée du programme de formation,  ainsi que les activités de travaux pratiques et d’évaluation qui y \nsont associés. \n \nObjectifs pédagogiques : \nCe cours vise à initier les étudiants à l'organisation anatomique du corps humain. À l'issue du cours, les \nétudiants doivent être capables de décrire les principaux organes et systèmes, de maîtriser le \nvocabulaire anatomique de base et de comprendre les re lations entre les structures anatomiques et \nleurs fonctions physiologiques. Le cours constitue un socle de connaissances indispensable pour les \nenseignements biomédicaux ultérieurs. \n \nCours repris dans la charge au moment du recrutement :  \nLe cours d’Anatomie humaine constitue l’une des deux activités d’apprentissage de l’unité \nd’enseignement « Anatomie et Embryologie » (4 crédits BIOL-F1712 : Th. 32 h, TP 12 h), aux côtés d’une \nactivité consacrée à l’embryologie humaine. L’activité d’apprentissage « Anatomie humaine » (S-BIOG-\n915) comprend 15 heures d'enseignement théorique, 5 heures de séminaires ainsi qu'une demi-journée \nde travaux pratiques. \nTitre requis  \nDocteur à thèse (PhD) dans un domaine des sciences biomédicales, médicales, ou de la santé ou en lien \navec la fonction \nCompétences requises \n• Expertise reconnue en anatomie humaine.\n   \n \n \n• Aptitude à travailler au sein d'une équipe pédagogique.  \n• Une expérience préalable d'enseignement universitaire dans le domaine constitue un atout. \nIntéressé·e ? \n \nDes renseignements complémentaires peuvent être obtenus auprès de Mme Cécile Moucheron \n(courriel : Eric.Bellefroid@ulb.be ). \n \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (si vous le souhaitez un CV type peut \nêtre téléchargé via le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-\net-scientifiques-cv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse URL \n(https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/3f-dossier-de-candidature-de-acad-tps-partiel-fh-docx).  \n \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants : \n \n• une lettre de motivation  \n• un dossier d’enseignement comprenant un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les \nactivités d’enseignement antérieures et un projet d’enseignement pour les 5 premières années du \nmandat, qui s’intègre de manière cohérente dans la vision de l’entit é de rattachement et dans les \nprofils d’enseignements des filières de formation auxquelles le candidat devra contribuer \n• les noms et adresses mail de contact de cinq personnes de référence susceptibles d’être contactées \npar les organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des genres.  Ces personnes ne \npeuvent être en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou affectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \nOù se rendre pour postuler ? \nCliquez ici : https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2093/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nPour tout problème de connexion ou question à propos de notre application, consultez notre FAQ : e-\nrecrut-mode-d-emploi-candidat-fr-_1734942952302-pdf \nN.B. : SAP respecte des directives européennes et états-uniennes, et en conséquence, n’autorise pas \nles accès à son application à partir des pays/ régions suivants : La Crimée, Sébastopol, République \npopulaire de Donetsk (DNR) / République populaire de Louhansk (LNR), Les zones non contrôlées par \nle gouvernement ukrainien dans les oblasts de Kherson et Zaporijia, Cuba, l’Iran, La Corée du Nord, la \nSyrie, la Russie et la Biélorussie. \nDès lors, les candidats qui postulent au départ de ces pays – et uniquement au départ de ces pays – \npeuvent envoyer leur curriculum vitae et leur dossier de candidature à cette adresse : rectrice@ulb.be \n \n \n \n   \n \nPolitique d’égalité des chances \nLa politique de gestion du personnel de l’ULB est axée sur la diversité et l’égalité des chances. \n \nNous recrutons les candidat·es  en fonction de leurs compétences, indépendamment de leur âge, leur \ngenre, leur orientation sexuelle, leur origine, leur nationalité, leurs convictions, leur handicap, etc. \nVous souhaitez bénéficier d’aménagements raisonnables dans le cadre de la procédure de sélection en \nraison d’un handicap, d’un trouble ou d’une maladie ? N’hésitez pas à prendre contact avec Marie Botty \n(marie.botty@ulb.be), notre personne de contact en charge des aspects de diversité pour le personnel \nenseignant et scientifique. Soyez assuré·e de la confidentialité de cette information. \n \nPlus de détails sur les politiques de genre et de diversité sont disponibles sur https://www.ulb.be/fr/l-\nulb-s-engage/diversites.  \n \n \n \nVous trouverez l’ensemble des dispositions relatives aux carrières du corps académique sur notre site à \nl’adresse http://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20362": {
      "title": "(1/20THS  OF A FULL-TIME POSITION, FOR A TOTAL VOLUME OF 15 HOURS/YEARS) FACULTY OF SCIENCES",
      "description": " \n  \n \n  \nSUBJECT TO THE APPROVAL BY THE ACADEMIC BOARD OF NOVEMBER 23TH,2026 \n  \nPART-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN HUMAN ANATOMY \n(1/20THS  OF A FULL-TIME POSITION, FOR A TOTAL VOLUME OF 15 HOURS/YEARS) \nFACULTY OF SCIENCES \n \n \nReference : 2027/A018 \nApplication deadline :  04/01/2027 12:00 PM  \nStart date : 01/10/2027 \nJob description \nThe Faculty of Science  invites applications for  a part-time academic position (0.05 FTE)  within the \nBachelor’s program in Biological Sciences, jointly organized by the University of Mons (UMons) and the \nUniversité libre de Bruxelles (ULB) on the Charleroi Ville Haute campus. \nThe successful candidate will be responsible for teaching a Human Anatomy course to first- and second-\nyear students  enrolled in the program, as well as conducting the associated  practical sessions  and \nassessment activities. \nEducational goals : \nThis course aims to introduce students to the anatomical organization of the human body. Upon \ncompletion of the course, students should be able to  describe the major organs and organ systems , \nmaster the basic anatomical terminology, and u nderstand the relationships between anatomical \nstructures and their physiological functions. \nThe course provides essential foundational knowledge for subsequent studies in the biomedical sciences \nand related disciplines. \nCourses covered at the time of recruitment:  \nThe Human Anatomy course is one of the two learning activities that make up the “Anatomy and \nEmbryology” teaching unit (4 ECTS credits; BIOL-F1712: 32 hours of lectures and 12 hours of practical \nsessions), alongside a complementary learning activity devoted to Human Embryology. \nThe Human Anatomy learning activity (S-BIOG-915) comprises 15 hours of lectures, 5 hours of \nseminars, and one half-day practical session.\n \n   \n \n \nQualifications required  \nPhD (Doctoral degree) in Biomedical Sciences, Medical Sciences, Health Sciences, or a related field \nrelevant to the position. \nSkills required  \n• Demonstrated expertise in human anatomy.  \n• Ability to work effectively as part of a teaching team.  \n• Previous experience in university-level teaching in the field is considered an asset. \nInterested ? \nFor more information, please contact Mr Eric Bellefroid (telephone: +32  2 650 97 32 – E-mail: \nEric.Bellefroid@ulb.be). \n \nYour application will consist of a Curriculum Vitae (if you wish, a standard CV can be downloaded from \nthe website: https: //www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-scientifiques-cv-type) \nand a document completed using the template available at this URL address  \nhttps://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/3e-applic-form-acad-tps-partiel-au-fh-docx.  \n \nThis template structures your application by including the following elements: \n• an application letter  \n• a teaching dossier including a 7,000-character report (4 pages) on the applicant's previous teaching \nactivities and a teaching project for the first five  years in this position; these must be relevant to \nthe faculty and to the teaching profiles for the programmes to which the applicant is to contribute \n• the names and e -mail addresses of five referees (respecting the gender balance) who may be \ncontacted by those in charge of evaluating applications.   These referees should not have conflicts \nof interest because of family or emotional ties. \nWhere to go to apply? \nClick here: https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2093/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nFor any connection problems or questions about our application, consult our FAQ : e-recrut-mode-d-\nemploi-candidat-en-_1734942996246-pdf \nN.B.: SAP complies with European and U.S. regulations and, as a result, does not allow access to its \napplication from the following countries/regions: Crimea, Sevastopol, the Donetsk People’s Republic \n(DNR) / Luhansk People’s Republic (LNR), areas not controlled by the Ukrainian government in the \nKherson and Zaporizhzhia regions, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Russia, and Belarus. \n  \nTherefore, candidates applying from these countries – and only from these countries – can submit \ntheir CV and application to this address: rectrice@ulb.be \n \nEqual opportunities policy \nULB's personnel management policy is geared towards diversity and equal opportunities. \n   \n \nWe recruit candidates on the basis of their skills, irrespective of age, gender, sexual orientation, origin, \nnationality, beliefs, disability, etc. \n \nWould you like to be provided with reasonable accommodation in the selection procedure because of \na disability, disorder, or illness?  Please contact Marie Botty, the person in charge of diversity aspects \nfor the academic and scientific staff (marie.botty@ulb.be). Be assured of the confidentiality of this \ninformation. \n \nMore details on the ULB gender and diversity policy are available at https://www.ulb.be/en/about-\nulb/gender-equality-at-ulb.  \n \n \n \n \nYou will find all the regulations relating to academic careers on our site at \nhttp://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20369": {
      "title": "POSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PARTIEL EN SCIENCE ET GESTION DE L’ENVIRONNEMENT",
      "description": " \n  \nSOUS RESERVE DE L’APPROBATION DU CONSEIL ACADEMIQUE DU 23 NOVEMBRE 2026 \n \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PARTIEL EN SCIENCE ET GESTION DE \nL’ENVIRONNEMENT  \n(CORRESPONDANT A 0,75/10 DE TEMPS PLEIN, SOIT UN FORFAIT HORAIRE DE 22,5 H/AN) \nFACULTE DES SCIENCES - DEPARTEMENT DES GEOSCIENCES, ENVIRONNEMENT ET SOCIETE \n \n \nRéférence : 2027/A023 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures :  04/01/2027 à midi \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 01/10/2027 \nDescriptif du poste \nUn poste académique à 0,075 ETP est offert au sein du Master en Science et Gestion de l’Environnement \n(MA-ENVIG), rattaché au Département des Géosciences, de l’Environnement et de la Société de la Faculté \ndes Sciences de l’Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB). \nCe poste à temps partiel sera associé au nouveau cours intégré au programme du Master dans le cadre de \nsa réforme, à partir de l’année académique 2027-2028 : ENVI-F-456 – «Limites planétaires et dynamiques \nsocio-environnementales» (Th. 36 h, Projet 20 h) . La personne recrutée rejoindra l’équipe des titulaires du \ncours et contribuera à son enseignement, à sa conception pédagogique ainsi qu’à son évaluation. \nLe Master en Science et Gestion de l’Environnement \nLe Master en Science et Gestion de l’Environnement ( MA-ENVIG) forme des professionnel·les  capables \nd’analyser les enjeux environnementaux contemporains et futurs et de contribuer à l’élaboration de \nréponses adaptées à ces enjeux. Le programme vise à fournir les connaissances, compétences et savoir -\nfaire nécessaires à une compréhension critique , interdisciplinaire et multidimensionnelle des \nproblématiques environnementales. \nLes enseignements combinent cours théoriques, exercices, séminaires et projets, ainsi que des mises en \nsituation et des confrontations avec la pratique, notamment par l’intervention de professionnel·les \nextérieur·es, les visites de terrain, les projets com mandités et les stages. Le Master vise notamment à \ndévelopper la capacité des étudiant·es  à comprendre, analyser et contribuer aux dynamiques socio -\nenvironnementales, du niveau local au niveau global, en mobilisant différentes perspectives et en prenant \nen compte la diversité des secteurs concernés. Les diplômé·es sont amené·es à exercer leurs compétences \ndans des entreprises, associations, ONG, institutions publiques, organisations politiques et organismes de \nrecherche. \nLe Master est principalement porté par SONYA et, plus largement, par le DGES. \nLe cours ENVI F456 – Limites planétaires et dynamiques socio-environnementales \nDans le cadre de la réforme du programme du MA -ENVIG, le cours « Limites planétaires et dynamiques \nsocio-environnementales » sera introduit à partir de l’année académique 2027-2028. Ce cours sera proposé \nen MA1, sous la forme d’un enseignement intensif d’une durée d’environ une semaine et demie, organisé \nau début du premier quadrimestre.\n   \n \n \nLe public étudiant se caractérise par une grande diversité de formations antérieures, comprenant \nnotamment les sciences humaines et sociales, les sciences, l’ingénierie et la gestion. Le cours a dès lors \npour objectif de permettre à l’ensemble des étudiant·es d’acquérir un socle commun de connaissances et \nde compétences et de disposer de repères partagés au début de leur formation de Master. Il s’agira \nnotamment de mettre en perspective les principaux défis environnementaux et de durabilité, ainsi que les \nmécanismes qui les sous -tendent. Le concept des limites planétaires constituera le cadre structurant du \ncours, en articulation avec d’autres cadres conceptuels pertinents. \nAprès une introduction générale au concept des limites planétaires et à ses relations avec d’autres \napproches, le cours approfondira les neuf limites planétaires. Le Prof. Frank Pattyn prendra en charge le \nvolet consacré au changement climatique. D’autres membres du département traiteront notamment de \nl’acidification des océans, des flux biogéochimiques, de l’évolution de l’eau douce et des ressources; etc. \nLe présent recrutement vise plus spécifiquement à assurer les enseignements relatifs à deux dimensions \nencore à couvrir : l’intégrité de la biosphère , dans ses dimensions fonctionnelle et génétique, et le \nchangement d’utilisation des terres. \nLa personne recrutée assurera 20 heures d’enseignement  théorique dans le cadre du cours, en \ncollaboration avec les autres titulaires, à savoir Wouter Achten (coordinateur et 24h), et Frank Pattyn (8h). \nElle participera également à la conception et à l’évaluation du cours, en collaboration avec l’équipe \nenseignante. \n \nProfil recherché \nL’ULB souhaite recruter un·e académique titulaire disposant d’une expertise permettant d’assurer les \nenseignements consacrés à ‘l’intégrité de la biosphère (biosphere integrity), dans ses dimensions \nfonctionnelle et génétique ; le changement d’utilisation des terres (land-system change). \nLa personne recrutée devra être en mesure d’inscrire ces enseignements dans les objectifs pédagogiques \ndu cours, dans l’approche interdisciplinaire du MA-ENVIG et dans les orientations scientifiques de SONYA. \nLe profil recherché répond idéalement aux critères suivants : \n• Une formation et/ou une expertise en biologie, écologie, biodiversité, sciences des écosystèmes, \nservices écosystémiques, systèmes, permettant d’aborder l’intégrité de la biosphère et le \nchangement d’utilisation des terres sous leurs dimensions scientifiques et techniques. \n• Une capacité à mettre en perspective ces connaissances avec les interactions entre sciences et \npolitiques publiques, aux niveaux national et international. \n• Une approche résolument interdisciplinaire, permettant de mettre son domaine d’expertise en \ndialogue avec d’autres disciplines, les enjeux sociétaux ainsi que les dynamiques socio -\nenvironnementales et socio-politiques. \n• Une capacité à inscrire son expertise dans une perspective plus large de durabilité et de \ntransformation socio-environnementale. \n• Une maîtrise suffisante du français pour assurer des enseignements universitaires et participer aux \nactivités pédagogiques du programme. \n• Une expérience confirmée de l’enseignement au niveau Master, idéalement dans un contexte \ninterdisciplinaire. \n• Une aptitude à collaborer au sein d’une équipe pédagogique et à assurer des enseignements en co-\ntitularité. \n \n   \n \nTitre requis  \nLe/la candidat.e aura accompli avec succès un Doctorat à thèse  dans un domaine pertinent pour les \nattentes d’enseignement décrit dans cette vacance.  \nIntéressé·e ? \nDes renseignements complémentaires peuvent être obtenus auprès de Tom Bauler et/ou Wouter Achten \n(tom.bauler@ulb.be ou wouter.achten@ulb.be). \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (si vous le souhaitez un CV type peut \nêtre téléchargé via le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-\nscientifiques-cv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse URL \n(https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/3f-dossier-de-candidature-de-acad-tps-partiel-fh-docx).  \n \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants : \n• une lettre de motivation  \n• un dossier d’enseignement  : un rapport de 5000 signes environ sur les activités d’enseignement \nantérieures (y compris les avis pédagogiques) , sur votre vision pédagogique,  ainsi qu’ un projet \nd’enseignement pour le course que le/la candidates intégrera (ENVI F 456 – Limites planétaires du MA \nENVI G) \n• les noms et adresses mail de contact de trois personnes de référence susceptibles d’être contactées par \nles organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des genres.  Ces personnes ne peuvent \nêtre en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou affectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \n \nOù se rendre pour postuler ? \nCliquez ici : https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2092/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nPour tout problème de connexion ou question à propos de notre application, consultez notre FAQ : e-\nrecrut-mode-d-emploi-candidat-fr-_1734942952302-pdf \nN.B. : SAP respecte des directives européennes et états-uniennes, et en conséquence, n’autorise pas les \naccès à son application à partir des pays/ régions suivants : La Crimée, Sébastopol, République populaire \nde Donetsk (DNR) / République populaire de Louhansk (LNR), Les zones non contrôlées par le \ngouvernement ukrainien dans les oblasts de Kherson et Zaporijia, Cuba, l’Iran, La Corée du Nord, la Syrie, \nla Russie et la Biélorussie. \nDès lors, les candidats qui postulent au départ de ces pays – et uniquement au départ de ces pays – \npeuvent envoyer leur curriculum vitae et leur dossier de candidature à cette adresse : rectrice@ulb.be \n \nPolitique d’égalité des chances \nLa politique de gestion du personnel de l’ULB est axée sur la diversité et l’égalité des chances. \n   \n \nNous recrutons les candidat·es en fonction de leurs compétences, indépendamment de leur âge, leur genre, \nleur orientation sexuelle, leur origine, leur nationalité, leurs convictions, leur handicap, etc. \nVous souhaitez bénéficier d’aménagements raisonnables dans le cadre de la procédure de sélection en \nraison d’un handicap, d’un trouble ou d’une maladie ? N’hésitez pas à prendre contact avec Marie Botty  \n(marie.botty@ulb.be), notre personne de contact en charge des aspects de diversité pour le personnel \nenseignant et scientifique. Soyez assuré·e de la confidentialité de cette information. \nPlus de détails sur les politiques de genre et de diversité sont disponibles sur https://www.ulb.be/fr/l-ulb-\ns-engage/diversites.  \n \n \nVous trouverez l’ensemble des dispositions relatives aux carrières du corps académique sur notre site à \nl’adresse http://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20370": {
      "title": "PART-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE AND MANAGEMENT",
      "description": " \n  \nSUBJECT TO THE APPROVAL BY THE ACADEMIC BOARD OF NOVEMBER 23TH,2026 \n \nPART-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE AND \nMANAGEMENT  \n(0,75/10THS OF A FULL-TIME POSITION, FOR A TOTAL VOLUME OF 22,5 HOURS/YEARS) \nFaculty of Sciences – Departement Geosciences, Environment and Society \n \n \nReference : 2027/A023 \nApplication deadline :  04/01/2027 12:00 PM \nStart date : 01/10/2027 \n \nJob description \nAn academic position at 0.075 FTE is available within the Master’s programme in Environmental Science \nand Management (MA -ENVIG), which is part of the Department of Geosciences, Environment and \nSociety (DGES) in the Faculty of Sciences at Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB). \nThis part -time position will be associated with a new course being introduced into the Master’s \ncurriculum as part of its reform, starting in the 2027 –2028 academic year: ENVI -F-456 – “ Limites \nplanétaires et dynamiques socio-environnementales ” (52 hours of lectures, 20 hours of project work). \nThe successful candidate will join the team of course instructors and contribute to teaching, course \ndesign and assessment. \nThe Master’s in Environmental Science and Management \nThe Master’s in Environmental Science and Management ( MA-ENVIG) trains professionals capable of \nanalysing current and future environmental challenges and contributing to the development of \nappropriate responses to these challenges. The programme aims to provide the knowledge, skills and \npractical expertise required for a critical, interdisciplinary and multid imensional understanding of \nenvironmental issues. \nTeaching combines theoretical courses, exercises, seminars and projects, as well as practical activities \nand opportunities to engage with real -world practice. These include contributions from external \nprofessionals, field visits, commissioned projects and internships. \nIn particular, the Master’s programme aims to develop students’ ability to understand, analyse and \ncontribute to socio -environmental dynamics at both local and global levels, drawing on different \nperspectives and taking into account  the diversity of sectors involved. Graduates go on to apply their \nskills in businesses, associations, non -governmental organisations (NGOs), public institutions, political \norganisations and research bodies. \nThe Master’s programme is primarily supported by SONYA and, more broadly, by the Department of \nGeosciences, Environment and Society (DGES). \nThe ENVI-F-456 course – Planetary Boundaries and Socio-Environmental Dynamics \nAs part of the reform of the MA -ENVIG curriculum, the course “Planetary Boundaries and Socio -\nEnvironmental Dynamics” will be introduced in the 2027–2028 academic year. It will be offered to first-\n \nyear Master’s students (MA1) as an intensive course lasting approximately one and a half weeks, \nscheduled at the beginning of the first semester. \nThe student cohort has a wide range of academic backgrounds, including the humanities and social \nsciences, natural sciences, engineering and management. The course therefore aims to ensure that all \nstudents acquire a common foundation of knowledge and skills and share a common frame of reference \nat the beginning of their Master’s studies. In particular, the course will place the major environmental \nand sustainability challenges, as well as the mechanisms underlying them, into perspective. The concept \nof planetary boundaries will provide the course’s overarching framework, in conju nction with other \nrelevant conceptual frameworks. \nFollowing a general introduction to the concept of planetary boundaries and its relationship to  other \napproaches, the course will examine the nine planetary boundaries in greater depth. Professor Frank \nPattyn will be responsible for the section on climate change. Other members of the department will \ncover topics including ocean acidification, biogeo chemical flows, changes in freshwater systems and \nresources, and other related subjects. \nThis recruitment is specifically intended to cover two areas that have yet to be addressed: biosphere \nintegrity, in both its functional and genetic dimensions, and land-use change. \nThe successful candidate will deliver 20 hours of lectures as part of the course, in collaboration with the \nother course instructors: Wouter Achten (course coordinator, 24 hours) and Frank Pattyn (8 hours). The \ncandidate will also participate in course design and assessment in collaboration with the teaching team. \nSkills required  \n \nULB wishes to recruit an academic staff member with expertise relevant to teaching the following \ntopics: biosphere integrity, in both its functional and genetic dimensions, and land-system change \n(land-use change). \n \nThe successful candidate must be able to integrate these topics into the course’s learning objectives, \nthe interdisciplinary approach of the MA-ENVIG programme, and SONYA’s scientific priorities. \n \nThe ideal candidate will meet the following criteria: \n• Academic background and expertise in biology, ecology, biodiversity, ecosystem science, \necosystem services, or systems science, enabling them to address biosphere integrity and land-use \nchange from scientific and technical perspectives. \n• Ability to contextualise this knowledge in relation to the interactions between science and public \npolicy at national and international levels. \n• A strong interdisciplinary approach, enabling them to engage their area of expertise in dialogue \nwith other disciplines, societal challenges, and socio-environmental and socio-political dynamics. \n• Ability to situate their expertise within a broader perspective on sustainability and socio-\nenvironmental transformation. \n• Sufficient proficiency in French to teach university-level courses and participate in the \nprogramme’s teaching activities. Applicants who do not speak French may be granted a period of \nadaptation, but they must be able to teach in French at the end of the third year following their \nappointment. \n• Demonstrated teaching experience at Master’s level, ideally in an interdisciplinary context. \n• Ability to collaborate within a teaching team and deliver courses jointly with other appointed \ninstructors. \n \n \nQualifications required \nPhD Degree (with doctoral thesis) in a field relevant for the teaching requirements outlined in this job \nvacancy.  \nInterested ? \nFor more information, please contact Tom Bauler and/or Wouter Achten (tom.bauler@ulb.be / \nwouter.achten@ulb.be). \nYour application will consist of a Curriculum Vitae(if you wish, a standard CV can be downloaded from \nthe website: https: //www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-scientifiques-cv-type) \nand a document completed using the template available at this URL address  \nhttps://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/3e-applic-form-acad-tps-partiel-au-fh-docx.  \n \nThis template structures your application by including the following elements: \n• an application letter  \n• A teaching portfolio, consisting of a report of approximately 5,000 characters outlining previous \nteaching activities (including teaching evaluations), the applicant’s teaching philosophy, and a \nteaching proposal for the course the successful candidate will contribute to (ENVI-F-456 – \nPlanetary Boundaries, part of the MA-ENVIG programme). \n• The names and email addresses of three referees who may be contacted by the bodies responsible \nfor evaluating applications. Gender balance should be taken into account when selecting referees. \nThese individuals must not have a conflict of interest arising from family or romantic relationships. \n \nIncomplete applications or applications that do not use the template provided will not be examined by \nthe selection committee. \nWhere to go to apply? \nClick here: https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2092/?isInternalUser=true \n \nFor any connection problems or questions about our application, consult our FAQ : e-recrut-mode-d-\nemploi-candidat-en-_1734942996246-pdf \nN.B.: SAP complies with European and U.S. regulations and, as a result, does not allow access to its \napplication from the following countries/regions: Crimea, Sevastopol, the Donetsk People’s Republic \n(DNR) / Luhansk People’s Republic (LNR), areas not controlled by the Ukrainian government in the \nKherson and Zaporizhzhia regions, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Russia, and Belarus. \n  \nTherefore, candidates applying from these countries – and only from these countries – can submit \ntheir CV and application to this address: rectrice@ulb.be \n \nEqual opportunities policy \nULB's personnel management policy is geared towards diversity and equal opportunities. \nWe recruit candidates on the basis of their skills, irrespective of age, gender, sexual orientation, origin, \nnationality, beliefs, disability, etc. \n \nWould you like to be provided with reasonable accommodation in the selection procedure because of \na disability, disorder, or illness?  Please contact Marie Botty, the person in charge of diversity aspects \nfor the academic and scientific staff (marie.botty@ulb.be). Be assured of the confidentiality of this \ninformation. \nMore details on the ULB gender and diversity policy are available at https://www.ulb.be/en/about-\nulb/gender-equality-at-ulb.  \n \n \nYou will find all the regulations relating to academic careers on our site at \nhttp://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20371": {
      "title": "POSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN ECOLOGIE COMPORTEMENTALE FACULTÉ DES SCIENCES",
      "description": " \n  \nSOUS RESERVE DE L’APPROBATION DU CONSEIL ACADEMIQUE DU 23 NOVEMBRE 2026 \n \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN ECOLOGIE COMPORTEMENTALE \nFACULTÉ DES SCIENCES   \nDEPARTEMENT DE BIOLOGIE DES ORGANISMES \n \n \nRéférence : 2027/A024 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures : 04/01/2027 à midi \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 01/10/2027 \nDescriptif du poste \nContexte du poste vacant \nCe poste est intégré au sein du Département de Biologie des Organismes (DBO) qui organise le \nBachelier en Sciences Biologiques et le Master en Biologie des Organismes et Ecologie. Au niveau de la \nrecherche le DBO compte 8 unités de recherche situées sur 3 campus (Solbosch, Plaine et Gosselies) \nhttps://sciences.ulb.be/departement-de-biologie-des-organismes/la-recherche-au-departement-de-\nbiologie-des-organismes): \n• Evolution Biologique et Ecologie (EBE), Campus du Solbosch, 8 professeurs \n• Biologie marine (BIOMAR), Campus du Solbosch, 1 professeur \n• Biologie moléculaire et évolution (MBE), Campus du Solbosch, 1 professeur \n• Biotechnologie végétale (LBV), Campus de Gosselies, 1 professeur \n• Écologie végétale et biogéochimie (EVB), Campus de La Plaine, 3 professeurs \n• Écologie sociale (USE), Campus de La Plaine, 2 professeurs \n• Écologie des systèmes et gestion des ressources (SERM), Campus de La Plaine, 2 professeurs \n• Herbarium de l'ULB (BRLU), cogéré par le personnel de l'EVB, de l'EBE et du SERM, Campus de La \nPlaine \nLe département compte également une cinquantaine de chercheurs et 9 techniciens de laboratoire.  \nL’étude du comportement animal est une force historique du DBO depuis plus de 50 ans.\n \nDomaine d’expertise recherché \n \nEcologie comportementale.  \n \nEn particulier (liste non exclusive) : \n• Écologie chimique et sensorielle (perception, communication, signaux) \n• Évolution du comportement  \n• Sélection sexuelle et stratégies reproductives \n• Comportement social et coopération \n• Conflits, dominance et hiérarchies sociales \n• Génétique du comportement \n• Interactions interspécifiques \n• Plasticité comportementale et stratégies adaptatives  \n• Réponses aux stress et aux changements environnementaux \n• Écologie comportementale de la conservation \n   \n \n• Modélisation du comportement et approches théoriques. \n \nUne dimension interdisciplinaire est un atout.  \n \nMissions \n \nRecherche \n• Développer un programme de recherche original et compétitif en écologie comportementale. \n• Publier régulièrement dans des revues scientifiques internationales à comité de lecture. \n• Obtenir des financements de recherche (nationaux et internationaux). \n• Encadrer des doctorant·e·s et post-doctorant·e·s. \n• Participer à des collaborations interdisciplinaires au sein et en dehors de l’université. \nEnseignement \n• S'intégrer dans les programmes d'enseignement du cursus en biologie des organismes et \nécologie, en particulier dans les enseignements consacrés au comportement animal. \n• Assurer des enseignements aux niveaux 1er cycle (bachelier) et 2e cycle (master). \n• Encadrer des mémoires de master. \n• Contribuer à l’innovation pédagogique et à la supervision de travaux pratiques et de terrain. \nService à la communauté \n• Participer aux activités administratives et collectives du département et de la faculté. \n• Contribuer au rayonnement scientifique de l’université (séminaires, conférences, \nvulgarisation scientifique). \n \nUne planification de ces missions à long terme (sur au moins 10 ans) est attendue. \n \n \nCours repris dans la charge au moment du recrutement \n \nAu niveau du Bachelier: \n• BIOL-F-103: Bases de la biologie des organismes (10 ECTS; partim cours magistral: 15h). Délai: à partir \nde l’année académique 2027-2028. \n• BIOL-F-304: Evolution et diversité des arthropodes et des vertébrés (5 ECTS; cours magistral: 24h). \nDélai : à partir de l’année académique 2028-2029. \n \nAu niveau du Master: \n• BIOL-F-446: Comportement animal (15 ECTS; partim cours magistral : 30h). Délai: progressivement au \ncours des 3 premières années. \n• BIOL-F-449: Biodiversité et conservation - écosystèmes terrestres et aquatiques (15 ECTS; partim \nexcursions: 40h). Délai: progressivement au cours des 3 premières années. \n•  Nouveau cours de master dans le domaine du candidat. Délai: à partir de l’année académique 2029-\n2030.  \n \nCette charge est susceptible d’évoluer en fonction des besoins du Département.  \n   \n \nTitre requis  \nDocteur à thèse en sciences biologiques au sens le plus large (tel que la biologie, la bio-ingénierie, les \nbiosciences, l'agronomie, les sciences de la vie et de la terre). \nCompétences requises \n• une ancienneté scientifique de 4 années minimum au moment de l’engagement, \n• une expérience post-doctorale, une mobilité en dehors de l’institution où a été réalisé le doctorat \net un excellent dossier scientifique seront des critères essentiels de sélection, \n• une expérience de recherche internationale sera un atout,  \n• être capable d’enseigner en français,  \n• un sens de l'organisation et des responsabilités, une capacité d'adaptation et de flexibilité, une \nfacilité de contact dans un contexte multiculturel, une autonomie et une capacité à travailler en \néquipe, un sens de l'initiative. \nIntéressé·e ? \nDes renseignements complémentaires peuvent être obtenus auprès du Prof. Jean-Christophe de Biseau \n(E-mail: jean.biseau@ulb.be) ou de Mme Catherine Buess (E-mail: secrdbo@ulb.be). \n \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (si vous le souhaitez un CV type peut \nêtre téléchargé via le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-\net-scientifiques-cv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse \nURL https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1f-dossier-de-candidature-acad-tps-plein-docx).  \n \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants :  \n• une lettre de motivation  \n• un dossier recherche de 7000 caractères (ou 4 pages) environ comprenant un rapport d’activités de \nrecherche et un projet de recherche, en ce compris l’insertion envisagée au sein des équipes de \nrecherche de l’ULB   \n• un dossier d’enseignement de 7000 caractères (ou 4 pages) environ comprenant un rapport \nd’activités d’enseignement antérieures et un projet d’enseignement pour les 5 premières années \ndu mandat, qui s’intègre de manière cohérente dans la vision de l’entité de rattachement et dans \nles profils d’enseignements des filières de formation auxquelles le candidat devra contribuer \n• une note sur les réalisations et projets internationaux (4 pages maximum) \n• les noms et adresses mail de contact de cinq personnes de référence susceptibles d’être \ncontactées par les organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des genres.  Ces \npersonnes ne peuvent être en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou affectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \n \nLa nomination, dans le cadre académique de I’ULB, se fait au rang de chargé de cours.  Dès leur \nnomination, les membres du corps académique sont autorisé·e·s à porter, à titre honorifique, le \nqualificatif de professeur·e. \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20372": {
      "title": "FULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN BEHAVIOURAL ECOLOGY FACULTY OF SCIENCES",
      "description": " \n  \nSUBJECT TO THE APPROVAL BY THE ACADEMIC BOARD OF NOVEMBER 23TH,2026 \n  \nFULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN BEHAVIOURAL ECOLOGY \n \nFACULTY OF SCIENCES   \nDEPARTMENT OF ORGANISMAL BIOLOGY \n \n \n \nReference : 2027/A024 \nApplication deadline: 04/01/2027 12:00 PM \nStart date: 01/10/2027  \nJob description  \nContext of the vacant position \nThis position is integrated within the Department of Organismal Biology (DBO), which is responsible for the \nBachelor's programme in Biological Sciences and the Master's programme in Organismal Biology and \nEcology. In terms of research, the DBO includes eight research units located across three campuses \n(Solbosch, Plaine and Gosselies): \n• Evolutionary Biology and Ecology (EBE), Solbosch Campus, 8 professors \n• Marine Biology (BIOMAR), Solbosch Campus, 1 professor \n• Molecular Biology and Evolution (MBE), Solbosch Campus, 1 professor \n• Plant Biotechnology (LBV), Gosselies Campus, 1 professor \n• Plant Ecology and Biogeochemistry (EVB), Plaine Campus, 3 professors \n• Social Ecology (USE), Plaine Campus, 2 professors \n• Systems Ecology and Resource Management (SERM), Plaine Campus, 2 professors \n• ULB Herbarium (BRLU), jointly managed by staff from EVB, EBE and SERM, Plaine Campus \n \nThe Department also includes approximately fifty researchers and nine laboratory technicians. \nAnimal behaviour research has been a historic strength of the DBO for more than 50 years. \n \nArea of Research \n \nBehavioural Ecology \n \nIn particular (non-exhaustive list): \n• Chemical and sensory ecology (perception, communication, signalling) \n• Behavioural evolution \n• Sexual selection and reproductive strategies \n• Social behaviour and cooperation \n• Conflict, dominance and social hierarchies \n• Behavioural genetics \n• Interspecific interactions \n• Behavioural plasticity and adaptive strategies \n• Responses to stress and environmental change \n• Conservation behavioural ecology \n \n• Behavioural modelling and theoretical approaches \n \nAn interdisciplinary dimension will be considered an asset. \n \nDuties \n \nResearch \n• Develop an original and competitive research programme in behavioural ecology. \n• Publish regularly in international peer-reviewed scientific journals. \n• Obtain national and international research funding. \n• Supervise PhD students and postdoctoral researchers. \n• Participate in interdisciplinary collaborations both within and outside the university. \nTeaching \n• Contribute to teaching within the Organismal Biology and Ecology curriculum, including in courses \ndevoted to animal behaviour. \n• Contribute to teaching at both undergraduate (bachelor's) and graduate (master's) levels. \n• Supervise master's theses. \n• Contribute to educational innovation and to the supervision of practical and field-based courses. \nService to the Community \n• Participate in the administrative and collective activities of the Department and Faculty. \n• Contribute to the university's scientific outreach and visibility (seminars, conferences, science \ncommunication). \n \nLong-term planning of these activities (over at least 10 years) is expected. \n \nCourses Included in the Teaching Load at the Time of Recruitment \n \nBachelor Level \n• BIOL-F-103: BIOL-F103: Bases de la biologie des organismes (10 ECTS; contribution to lectures: 15h). \nTimeline: from academic year 2027-2028. \n• BIOL-F-304: Evolution et diversité des arthropodes et des vertébrés (5 ECTS; contribution to lectures: \n24h). \nTimeline: from academic year 2028-2029. \nMaster Level \n• BIOL-F-446: Animal Behaviour (15 ECTS; contribution to lectures: 30h). \nTimeline: gradually during the first three years. \n• BIOL-F-449: Biodiversity and Conservation - Terrestrial and Aquatic Ecosystems (15 ECTS; contribution to \nfield excursions: 40h). \nTimeline: gradually during the first three years. \n• New master's course in the candidate's area of expertise. \nTimeline: from academic year 2029-2030. \n \nThis teaching load may evolve with the needs of the Department. \nQualifications required  \nPhD in Biological Sciences in the broadest sense (including biology, bioengineering, biosciences, agronomy, \nlife sciences and earth sciences). \n \n \nSkills required  \n• A minimum of four years of scientific seniority at the time of appointment. \n• Postdoctoral experience, mobility outside the institution where the PhD was obtained, and an \nexcellent scientific record will be essential selection criteria. \n• International research experience will be considered an asset. \n• Ability to teach in French. \n• Strong organisational and leadership skills, adaptability and flexibility, ease of interaction in a \nmulticultural environment, autonomy, ability to work collaboratively, and initiative. \nInterested? \nFurther information may be obtained from: \nProf. Jean-Christophe de Biseau \nE-mail: jean.biseau@ulb.be \nor \nMs Catherine Buess \nE-mail: secrdbo@ulb.be \n \nYour application will consist of a Curriculum Vitae (if you wish, a standard CV can be downloaded from the \nwebsite: https: //www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-scientifiques-cv-type) and a \ndocument completed using the template available at this URL address  \nhttps://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1e-applic-form-acad-tps-plein-docx.  \n \nThis template structures the application around the following components: \n• An application letter. \n• A research document of approximately 7,000 characters (or 4 pages), including a report of \nprevious research activities and a research project, and including the proposed integration within \nULB research teams. \n• A teaching document of approximately 7,000 characters (or 4 pages), including a report of \nprevious teaching activities and a teaching project for the first five years of the mandate, \ncoherently integrated into the vision of the host entity and the educational profiles of the \nprogrammes to which the candidate will contribute. \n• A statement on international achievements and projects (maximum 4 pages). \n• Names and e-mail addresses of five referees who may be contacted by the committees \nresponsible for evaluating applications, with attention paid to gender balance. These referees \nmust not be in a conflict of interest due to family or personal relationships. \n \nIncomplete applications, or applications not using the provided template, will not be considered by the \nselection committee. \n \nThe appointment to the academic staff of ULB is made at ”Chargé de Cours” level. As of their appointment, \nmembers of academic staff are authorised to use the honorary title of ”Professeur”. \nWhere to go to apply? \nClick here: https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2090/?isInternalUser=true \n \nFor any connection problems or questions about our application, consult our FAQ : e-recrut-mode-d-\nemploi-candidat-en-_1734942996246-pdf \n \nN.B.: SAP complies with European and U.S. regulations and, as a result, does not allow access to its \napplication from the following countries/regions: Crimea, Sevastopol, the Donetsk People’s Republic (DNR) \n/ Luhansk People’s Republic (LNR), areas not controlled by the Ukrainian government in the Kherson and \nZaporizhzhia regions, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Russia, and Belarus.  \n \nTherefore, candidates applying from these countries – and only from these countries – can submit their CV \nand application to this address: rectrice@ulb.be \n \nEqual opportunities policy \nULB's personnel management policy is geared towards diversity and equal opportunities. \nWe recruit candidates on the basis of their skills, irrespective of age, gender, sexual orientation, origin, \nnationality, beliefs, disability, etc. \nWould you like to be provided with reasonable accommodation in the selection procedure because of a \ndisability, disorder, or illness?  Please contact Marie Botty, the person in charge of diversity aspects for the \nacademic and scientific staff (marie.botty@ulb.be). Be assured of the confidentiality of this information. \nMore details on the ULB gender and diversity policy are available at Diversity at ULB - ULB. \n \nYou will find all the regulations relating to academic careers on our site at \nhttp://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20365": {
      "title": "POSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN IMMUNOLOGIE, MICROBIOLOGIE, OU INTERACTIONS HOTE-MICROORGANISMES",
      "description": " \n  \nSOUS RESERVE DE L’APPROBATION DU CONSEIL ACADEMIQUE DU 23 NOVEMBRE 2026 \n \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN IMMUNOLOGIE, MICROBIOLOGIE, OU \nINTERACTIONS HOTE-MICROORGANISMES   \nFACULTE DES SCIENCES \n \n \n \nRéférence : 2027/A020 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures :  04/01/2027 à midi \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 01/10/2027 \nDescriptif du poste \nLe Département de Biologie Moléculaire (DBM) de l’Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB) ouvre un poste \nacadémique à temps plein au sein de son département de recherche et d’enseignement \npluridisciplinaire. \n \nDomaine de recherche \n \nLa ou le candidat·e recruté.e étudiera les mécanismes moléculaires et cellulaires qui régissent la biologie \ndes microorganismes et/ou le fonctionnement du système immunitaire, en s'appuyant sur des \napproches expérimentales de pointe ou interdisciplinaires. Nous encourageons particuliè rement les \nprojets de recherche fondamentale, guidés par la curiosité scientifique, visant à approfondir notre \ncompréhension des processus biologiques, indépendamment de leurs applications cliniques ou \ntranslationnelles immédiates. \n \nLes domaines de recherche envisagés comprennent notamment, mais sans s'y limiter : \n \nMicrobiologie fondamentale \n \n• Physiologie et métabolisme des microorganismes \n• Génétique microbienne, régulation de l'expression génique et évolution des génomes \n• Mécanismes moléculaires de l'adaptation des microorganismes et des réponses aux stress \n \nImmunologie fondamentale \n \n• Régulation, différenciation et ontogénie des cellules immunitaires \n• Contrôle transcriptionnel, épigénétique et métabolique des réponses immunitaires \n• Mécanismes fondamentaux de l'inflammation, de la tolérance et de l'immunopathologie \n \nÀ l'interface de la microbiologie et de l'immunologie \n \n• Mécanismes moléculaires des interactions hôte-microorganismes \n \n   \n \n• Adaptation réciproque de l'hôte et des microorganismes dans les contextes physiologiques \net pathologiques  \n• Organisation et dynamique des écosystèmes hôte-microorganismes \n \n \nLes candidatures de scientifiques travaillant sur divers modèles expérimentaux et utilisant des \napproches innovantes en biologie moléculaire et cellulaire, génétique, génomique fonctionnelle, \nbiochimie ou biologie computationnelle , biologie des systèmes et technologies multi -omiques sont \nvivement encouragées. \n \nLa ou le candidat·e rejoindra le Département de Biologie Moléculaire au sein du Brussels South Charleroi \nBiopark, un environnement très dynamique dédié aux sciences de la vie : https://biopark.be/en. Le \nBioPark abrite trois instituts de recherche académique et offre des infrastructures de laboratoire à la \npointe de la technologie, ainsi qu’un réseau florissant de plus de 100 entreprises du secteur des sciences \nde la vie. Dans ce cadre, le candidat pourra collaborer de manière interdisciplinaire, en travaillant avec \ndes experts en biologie des acides nucléiques, microbiologie, immunologie, virologie, parasitologie, ainsi \nqu’en biologie cellulaire et du développement. \n \nLa ou le candidat·e  bénéficiera d'un environnement scientifique particulièrement propice au \ndéveloppement de recherches à l'interface entre immunologie et microbiologie, grâce à la présence au \nsein du département de groupes de recherche complémentaires couvrant l'immunologie , la \nmicrobiologie, la virologie, la parasitologie, la génétique et la biologie des acides nucléiques. Les projets \nfavorisant les synergies entre ces disciplines seront particulièrement encouragés. \n \nObjectifs pédagogiques et scientifiques \n \nLa ou le candidat·e devra faire preuve d’une forte motivation et de solides compétences en matière \nd’enseignement et d’encadrement. Il contribuera aux activités pédagogiques dans un large éventail de \ndomaines modernes de la biochimie, de la biologie moléculaire et cellulaire, dans les programmes de \nBachelier et de Master, en assurant à la fois des cours fondamentaux et des cours spécialisés. \nL’encadrement d’étudiants de premier et deuxième cycles  ainsi que de chercheurs postdoctoraux est \négalement attendu. Pour les candidats ne maîtrisant pas le français, une période temporaire \nd’apprentissage du français et d’enseignement en anglais pourra être accordée pour une durée \nmaximale de trois ans, après quoi le candidat devra être en mesure d’enseigner en français. \n \nLe candidat devra diriger un programme de recherche indépendant (principal investigator) et compétitif \net assurer son financement par des subventions externes (fonds européens et régionaux, par exemple \nERC, Wel-RI, FNRS, etc.). \n \nCours repris dans la charge au moment du recrutement : \n \n• BIOL-Y-331    Interactions hôte-pathogènes  \n5 ECTS (Cours magistral  : 14h, Exercices dirigés  : 24h, \nTravaux pratiques : 24h, Travaux personnels : 30h) \nCharge : Cours magistral : 14h, Exercices dirigés : 24h, Travaux personnels : 30h. \n \n• BIOL-F-104/BIOL-F-105/CHIM-F-208 Bases Moléculaires du vivant \n   \n \n10 ECTS (Cours magistral : 64h,  Exercices dirigés : \n20h, Travaux pratiques : 12 h)  \n \nCharge : Cours magistral : 14h (partagé par les sections Biologie/Bioingénieur/Chimie)  \n \n• BIOL-F-303    Laboratoires de biologie moléculaire  \n5 ECTS (Travaux pratiques : 48h) \nCharge : Travaux pratiques : 48h  \n \nTitre requis  \nDocteur à thèse en sciences biologiques ou biomédicales, médecine ou sciences pharmaceutiques, ou \ndisciplines apparentées.  \nCompétences requises \n• Vous avez une ancienneté scientifique de 4 années minimum au moment de l’engagement. \n• Vous pouvez faire état d’une expérience post-doctorale et d’un excellent dossier scientifique. \n• Vous avez démontré votre capacité à mener des recherches originales de grande qualité, en \nadéquation avec votre niveau de carrière. \n• Si vous avez effectué une mobilité en dehors de l’institution où a été réalisé votre doctorat (durant \nla période doctorale ou après), ce sera pris en compte lors de l’évaluation de votre dossier. \n• Si vous ne parlez pas couramment la langue française (niveau C1), une période d’adaptation peut \nvous être accordée, mais vous devrez être capable d’enseigner en français à la fin de la troisième \nannée suivant votre nomination. \n• L’expérience d’enseignement sera prise en compte et valorisée.  \nIntéressé·e ? \nDes renseignements complémentaires peuvent être obtenus auprès des Prof. Stanislas Goriely et \nLaurence Van Melderen (courriel : Stanislas.Goriely@ulb.be, Laurence.Vanmelderen@ulb.be). \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (si vous le souhaitez un CV type peut \nêtre téléchargé via le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-\net-scientifiques-cv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse \nURL https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1f-dossier-de-candidature-acad-tps-plein-docx).  \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants :  \n• une lettre de motivation  \n• un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les activités de recherche et un projet de \nrecherche, en ce compris l’insertion envisagée au sein des équipes de recherche de l’ULB   \n• un dossier d’enseignement comprenant un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les \nactivités d’enseignement antérieures et un projet d’enseignement pour les 5 premières années \ndu mandat, qui s’intègre de manière cohérente dans la vision de l’entité de rattachement et \ndans les profils d’enseignements des filières de formation auxquelles le candidat devra \ncontribuer \n• une note sur les réalisations et projets internationaux (4 pages maximum) \n   \n \n• les noms et adresses mail de contact de cinq personnes de référence susceptibles d’être \ncontactées par les organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des \ngenres.  Ces personnes ne peuvent être en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou \naffectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \n \nLa nomination, dans le cadre académique de I’ULB, se fait au rang de chargé de cours.  Dès leur \nnomination, les membres du corps académique sont autorisé·e·s à porter, à titre honorifique, le \nqualificatif de professeur·e. \n \nOù se rendre pour postuler ? \nCliquez ici : https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2091/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nPour tout problème de connexion ou question à propos de notre application, consultez notre FAQ : e-\nrecrut-mode-d-emploi-candidat-fr-_1734942952302-pdf \nN.B. : SAP respecte des directives européennes et états-uniennes, et en conséquence, n’autorise pas \nles accès à son application à partir des pays/ régions suivants : La Crimée, Sébastopol, République \npopulaire de Donetsk (DNR) / République populaire de Louhansk (LNR), Les zones non contrôlées par \nle gouvernement ukrainien dans les oblasts de Kherson et Zaporijia, Cuba, l’Iran, La Corée du Nord, la \nSyrie, la Russie et la Biélorussie. \nDès lors, les candidats qui postulent au départ de ces pays – et uniquement au départ de ces pays – \npeuvent envoyer leur curriculum vitae et leur dossier de candidature à cette adresse : rectrice@ulb.be \n \nPolitique d’égalité des chances \nLa politique de gestion du personnel de l’ULB est axée sur la diversité et l’égalité des chances. \nNous recrutons les candidat·es en fonction de leurs compétences, indépendamment de leur âge, leur \ngenre, leur orientation sexuelle, leur origine, leur nationalité, leurs convictions, leur handicap, etc. \nVous souhaitez bénéficier d’aménagements raisonnables dans le cadre de la procédure de sélection en \nraison d’un handicap, d’un trouble ou d’une maladie ? N’hésitez pas à prendre contact avec Marie \nBotty (marie.botty@ulb.be) notre personne de contact en charge des aspects de diversité pour le \npersonnel enseignant et scientifique. Soyez assuré·e de la confidentialité de cette information. \nPlus de détails sur les politiques de genre et de diversité sont disponibles sur https://www.ulb.be/fr/l-\nulb-s-engage/diversites.  \n \n \nVous trouverez l’ensemble des dispositions relatives aux carrières du corps académique sur notre site \nà l’adresse http://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20366": {
      "title": "FULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN IMMUNOLOGY, MICROBIOLOGY, OR HOST–MICROORGANISM INTERACTIONS",
      "description": " \n  \nSUBJECT TO THE APPROVAL BY THE ACADEMIC BOARD OF NOVEMBER 23TH,2026 \n  \nFULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN IMMUNOLOGY, \nMICROBIOLOGY, OR HOST–MICROORGANISM INTERACTIONS \n \nFACULTY OF SCIENCES \n \n \nReference : 2027/A020 \nApplication deadline: 04/01/2027 12:00 PM \nStart date: 01/10/2027  \nJob description  \nThe Department of Molecular Biology (DBM) at the Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB) is inviting \napplications for a full-time academic position within its multidisciplinary research and teaching department. \n \nArea of Research   \n \nThe successful candidate will investigate the molecular and cellular mechanisms governing microorganism \nbiology and/or immune system function, using cutting-edge experimental or interdisciplinary approaches.  \n \nWe particularly encourage curiosity-driven basic research projects aimed at deepening our understanding \nof biological processes, regardless of their immediate clinical or translational applications. \n \nResearch areas of interest include, but are not limited to: \n \nFundamental Microbiology \n \n• Microbial physiology and metabolism \n• Microbial genetics, regulation of gene expression, and genome evolution \n• Molecular mechanisms underlying microbial adaptation and stress responses \n \nFundamental Immunology \n \n• Regulation, differentiation, and ontogeny of immune cells \n• Transcriptional, epigenetic, and metabolic control of immune responses \n• Fundamental mechanisms of inflammation, tolerance, and immunopathology \n \nAt the Interface of Microbiology and Immunology \n \n• Molecular mechanisms underlying host-microorganism interactions \n• Reciprocal adaptation of hosts and microorganisms in physiological and pathological contexts \n• Organization and dynamics of host-microorganism ecosystems \n \nApplications from scientists working with diverse experimental models and employing innovative \napproaches in molecular and cellular biology, genetics, functional genomics, biochemistry, computational \nbiology, systems biology, or multi-omics technologies are strongly encouraged. \n \nThe successful candidate will join the Department of Molecular Biology at the Brussels South Charleroi \nBiopark, a highly dynamic life sciences environment: https://biopark.be/en. The BioPark is home to three \nacademic research institutes and provides state-of-the-art laboratory facilities, as well as a thriving network \nof more than 100 companies in the life sciences sector. This environment offers opportunities for \ninterdisciplinary collaboration with experts in nucleic acid biology, microbiology, immunology, virology, \nparasitology, and cell and developmental biology. \n \nThe successful candidate will benefit from a particularly stimulating scientific environment for developing \nresearch at the interface of immunology and microbiology. The department hosts complementary research \ngroups specializing in immunology, microbiology, virology, parasitology, genetics, and nucleic acid biology. \nResearch projects fostering synergies across these disciplines will be particularly encouraged. \n \n \nEducational and scientific goals : \n \nThe successful candidate will demonstrate strong motivation and proven skills in teaching and mentoring. \nThey will contribute to teaching activities across a broad range of contemporary topics in biochemistry and \nmolecular and cellular biology at both Bachelor’s and Master’s levels, delivering both fundamental and \nspecialized courses. They will also be expected to supervise undergraduate and graduate students, as well \nas postdoctoral researchers. \n \nFor candidates who are not proficient in French, a temporary period of French-language training, during \nwhich teaching may be conducted in English, may be granted for a maximum of three years. By the end of \nthis period, the candidate must be able to teach in French. \n \nThe successful candidate will lead an independent and competitive research programme as a principal \ninvestigator (PI) and secure external funding to support it, including European and regional grants and \nfunding schemes such as the ERC, Wel-RI, and FNRS. \n \n \nCourses covered at the time of recruitment : \n \n• BIOL-Y-331  Host-Pathogen Interactions \n5 ECTS (Lectures: 14 hours; Tutorials: 24 hours; Practical laboratory sessions: 24 hours; \nIndependent study: 30 hours) \nTeaching load: Lectures: 14 hours; Tutorials: 24 hours; Independent study: 30 hours. \n \n• BIOL-F-104 / BIOL-F-105 / CHIM-F-208  Molecular Basis of Life \n10 ECTS (Lectures: 64 hours; Tutorials: 20 hours; Practical laboratory sessions: 12 hours) \nTeaching load: Lectures: 14 hours (shared across the Biology, Bioengineering, and Chemistry \nprogrammes). \n \n• BIOL-F-303 Molecular Biology Laboratory \n5 ECTS (Practical laboratory sessions: 48 hours) \nTeaching load: Practical laboratory sessions: 48 hours. \n \n \n \nQualifications required : \nPhD Degree (with doctoral thesis) in biological or biomedical sciences, medicine, pharmaceutical sciences, \nor a related discipline.  \nSkills required  \n• Applicants should have at least 4 years of research experience at the time of their recruitment. \n• Post-doctoral experience and an excellent scientific record are a plus. \n• Demonstrated ability to conduct original, high-quality research commensurate with your career stage. \n• Exchange periods outside of the applicants’ home institution (during or after their PhD) will be taken \ninto consideration when evaluating applications. \n• Applicants who do not speak French (level C1) may be granted a period of adaptation, but they must be \nable to teach in French at the end of the third year following their appointment. \n• Teaching experience will be taken into consideration and viewed favorably.  \nInterested ? \nFor more information, please contact Prof. Stanislas Goriely or Laurence Van Melderen  (E-mail: \nstanislas.goriely@ulb.be, Laurence.vanmelderen@ulb.be). \nYour application will consist of a Curriculum Vitae(if you wish, a standard CV can be downloaded from the \nwebsite: https: //www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-scientifiques-cv-type) and a \ndocument completed using the template available at this URL address  \nhttps://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1e-applic-form-acad-tps-plein-docx.  \n \nThis template structures your application by including the following elements: \n• an application letter  \n• a 7,000-character report (4 pages) presenting the applicant’s research activities and a research \nproject, including how these will integrate into ULB’s research teams \n• a teaching dossier including a 7,000-character report (4 pages) on the applicant's previous teaching \nactivities and a teaching project for the first five years in this position; these must be relevant to the \nfaculty and to the teaching profiles for the programmes to which the applicant is to contribute \n• a note on the applicant's international achievements and projects (no more than 4 pages) \n• the names and e-mail addresses of five referees (respecting the gender balance) who may be \ncontacted by those in charge of evaluating applications.  These referees should not have conflicts of \ninterest because of family or emotional ties. \n \nIncomplete applications or applications that do not use the template provided will not be examined by the \nselection committee. \n \nThe appointment to the academic staff of ULB is made at ”Chargé de Cours” level. As of their appointment, \nmembers of academic staff are authorised to use the honorary title of ”Professeur”. \nWhere to go to apply? \nClick here: https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2091/?isInternalUser=true \n \nFor any connection problems or questions about our application, consult our FAQ : e-recrut-mode-d-\nemploi-candidat-en-_1734942996246-pdf \n \n \nN.B.: SAP complies with European and U.S. regulations and, as a result, does not allow access to its \napplication from the following countries/regions: Crimea, Sevastopol, the Donetsk People’s Republic (DNR) \n/ Luhansk People’s Republic (LNR), areas not controlled by the Ukrainian government in the Kherson and \nZaporizhzhia regions, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Russia, and Belarus.  \n \nTherefore, candidates applying from these countries – and only from these countries – can submit their CV \nand application to this address: rectrice@ulb.be \n \nEqual opportunities policy \nULB's personnel management policy is geared towards diversity and equal opportunities. \nWe recruit candidates on the basis of their skills, irrespective of age, gender, sexual orientation, origin, \nnationality, beliefs, disability, etc. \nWould you like to be provided with reasonable accommodation in the selection procedure because of a \ndisability, disorder, or illness?  Please contact Marie Botty, the person in charge of diversity aspects for the \nacademic and scientific staff (marie.botty@ulb.be). Be assured of the confidentiality of this information. \nMore details on the ULB gender and diversity policy are available at Diversity at ULB - ULB. \n \n \nYou will find all the regulations relating to academic careers on our site at \nhttp://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20367": {
      "title": "POSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN BIOLOGIE DEVELOPPEMENTALE FACULTE DES SCIENCES",
      "description": " \n  \nSOUS RESERVE DE L’APPROBATION DU CONSEIL ACADEMIQUE DU 23 NOVEMBRE 2026 \n \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN BIOLOGIE DEVELOPPEMENTALE \nFACULTE DES SCIENCES \n \n \n \nRéférence : 2027/A022 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures :  04/01/2027 à midi \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 01/10/2027 \nDescriptif du poste \nLe Département de Biologie Moléculaire (DBM) de la Faculté des Science de l’Université libre de \nBruxelles (ULB) recrute un académique à temps plein pour rejoindre un environnement de recherche et \nd’enseignement pluridisciplinaire. \n \nDomaine de recherche :  \n \nLes candidats possédant un parcours scientifique internationalement reconnu et un programme de \nrecherche innovant en biologie développementale animale sont invités à postuler. La priorité sera \ndonnée aux candidats dont les activités de recherche s’intègrent dans les thématiques du département \net sont susceptibles d’en renforcer les axes existants, en particulier dans les domaines de la biologie du \ndéveloppement du système nerveux ou cardiovasculaire. \n \nLe candidat rejoindra le Département de Biologie Moléculaire au sein du Brussels South Charleroi \nBiopark, un environnement très dynamique dédié aux sciences de la vie : https://biopark.be/en. Le \nBioPark abrite trois instituts de recherche académique et offre des infrastructures de laboratoire à la \npointe de la technologie, ainsi qu’un réseau florissant de plus de 100 entreprises du secteur des sciences \nde la vie. Dans ce cadre, le candidat aura l’opportunité de développer des collaborations \ninterdisciplinaires avec des experts en biologie cellulaire et du développement, biologie des acides \nnucléiques, microbiologie, immunologie, virologie et parasitologie. \n \nObjectifs pédagogiques et scientifiques : \n \nLe candidat devra faire preuve d’une forte motivation et de solides compétences en matière \nd’enseignement et d’encadrement. Il contribuera aux activités pédagogiques  principalement centrées \nsur la biologie du développement, dans les programmes de Bachelier et de Master, en assurant à la fois \ndes cours fondamentaux et des cours spécialisés. L’encadrement d’étudiants de premier et deuxième \ncycles ainsi que de chercheurs postdoctoraux est également attendu. Pour les candidats ne maîtrisant \npas le français, une période temporaire d’apprentissage du français et d’enseignement en anglais pourra \nêtre accordée pour une durée maximale de trois ans, après quoi le candidat devra être en mesure \nd’enseigner en français. \nLe candidat devra diriger un programme de recherche compétitif et assurer son financement par des \nsubventions externes (fonds européens et régionaux, par exemple ERC, Wel-RI, FNRS, etc.).\n \n \nCours repris dans la charge au moment du recrutement :      \n \n• BIOL-F-318 – Histophysiologie et développement animal : 5 ECTS (partim), BA3, 18 h de cours \nthéorique, co-titulaire. \n• BIOL-F-320 – Travaux pratiques d’histopathologie et développement animal : 5 ECTS (partim), \nBA3, 24 h de travaux pratiques, cours à option, coordinateur. \n• S-BIOG-935 – Biologie du développement (correspond aux deux intitulés précédents dupliqués \nsur le site de Charleroi): 5 ECTS, BA3, cours et travaux pratiques, coordinateur. \n• S-BIOG-914 – Embryologie humaine : 5 ECTS (partim), BA1–BA2, 12 h de cours et 8 h de \ntravaux pratiques, partim, coordinateur. \n• BMOL-F-419 – Neurosciences et biologie cardiovasculaire : 5 ECTS (partim), Master 1, 12 h de \ncours et séminaires, cours à option, co-titulaire. \n \nEnseignement optionnel : \n \n• BMOL-F-4008 – Travaux pratiques de biologie moléculaire : 5 ECTS, Master 1, 48 h de travaux \npratiques, TP à option. \n \nTitre requis  \nDocteur à thèse en sciences biologiques ou biomédicales, médecine ou sciences pharmaceutiques, ou \ndisciplines apparentées.  \nCompétences requises \n• Vous avez une ancienneté scientifique de 4 années minimum (postdoctoral) au moment de \nl’engagement. \n• Vous pouvez faire état d’une expérience post-doctorale et d’un excellent dossier scientifique. \n• Vous avez démontré votre capacité à mener des recherches originales de grande qualité, en \nadéquation avec votre niveau de carrière. \n• Si vous avez effectué une mobilité en dehors de l’institution où a été réalisé votre doctorat (durant la \npériode doctorale ou après), cela sera pris en compte lors de l’évaluation de votre dossier. \n• Si vous ne parlez pas couramment la langue française (niveau C1), une période d’adaptation peut \nvous être accordée, mais vous devrez être capable d’enseigner en français à la fin de la troisième \nannée suivant votre nomination. \n• L’expérience d’enseignement sera prise en compte et valorisée.  \nIntéressé·e ? \nDes renseignements complémentaires peuvent être obtenus auprès du Prof. Maud Martin (courriel : \nmaud.martin@ulb.be). \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (si vous le souhaitez un CV type peut \nêtre téléchargé via le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-\nscientifiques-cv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse URL \nhttps://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1f-dossier-de-candidature-acad-tps-plein-docx).  \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants :  \n• une lettre de motivation  \n• un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les activités de recherche et un projet de \nrecherche, en ce compris l’insertion envisagée au sein des équipes de recherche de l’ULB   \n \n• un dossier d’enseignement comprenant un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les \nactivités d’enseignement antérieures et un projet d’enseignement pour les 5 premières années du \nmandat, qui s’intègre de manière cohérente dans la vision de l’entité de rattachement et dans les \nprofils d’enseignements des filières de formation auxquelles le candidat devra contribuer \n• une note sur les réalisations et projets internationaux (4 pages maximum) \n• les noms et adresses mail de contact de cinq personnes de référence susceptibles d’être \ncontactées par les organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des genres.  Ces \npersonnes ne peuvent être en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou affectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \n \nLa nomination, dans le cadre académique de I’ULB, se fait au rang de chargé de cours.  Dès leur \nnomination, les membres du corps académique sont autorisé·e·s à porter, à titre honorifique, le \nqualificatif de professeur·e. \n \nOù se rendre pour postuler ? \nCliquez ici : https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2089/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nPour tout problème de connexion ou question à propos de notre application, consultez notre FAQ : e-\nrecrut-mode-d-emploi-candidat-fr-_1734942952302-pdf \nN.B. : SAP respecte des directives européennes et états-uniennes, et en conséquence, n’autorise pas les \naccès à son application à partir des pays/ régions suivants : La Crimée, Sébastopol, République populaire \nde Donetsk (DNR) / République populaire de Louhansk (LNR), Les zones non contrôlées par le \ngouvernement ukrainien dans les oblasts de Kherson et Zaporijia, Cuba, l’Iran, La Corée du Nord, la Syrie, \nla Russie et la Biélorussie. \nDès lors, les candidats qui postulent au départ de ces pays – et uniquement au départ de ces pays – \npeuvent envoyer leur curriculum vitae et leur dossier de candidature à cette adresse : rectrice@ulb.be \nPolitique d’égalité des chances \nLa politique de gestion du personnel de l’ULB est axée sur la diversité et l’égalité des chances. \nNous recrutons les candidat·es en fonction de leurs compétences, indépendamment de leur âge, leur \ngenre, leur orientation sexuelle, leur origine, leur nationalité, leurs convictions, leur handicap, etc. \nVous souhaitez bénéficier d’aménagements raisonnables dans le cadre de la procédure de sélection en \nraison d’un handicap, d’un trouble ou d’une maladie ? N’hésitez pas à prendre contact avec Marie Botty \n(marie.botty@ulb.be) notre personne de contact en charge des aspects de diversité pour le personnel \nenseignant et scientifique. Soyez assuré·e de la confidentialité de cette information. \nPlus de détails sur les politiques de genre et de diversité sont disponibles sur https://www.ulb.be/fr/l-\nulb-s-engage/diversites.  \n \n \nVous trouverez l’ensemble des dispositions relatives aux carrières du corps académique sur notre site à \nl’adresse http://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20368": {
      "title": "FULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN DEVELOPMENTAL BIOLOGY FACULTY OF SCIENCES",
      "description": " \n  \nSUBJECT TO THE APPROVAL BY THE ACADEMIC BOARD OF NOVEMBER 23TH,2026 \n \nFULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN DEVELOPMENTAL BIOLOGY \nFACULTY OF SCIENCES \n \n \n \nRéférence : 2027/A022  \nApplication deadline :  04/01/2027 à midi \nExpected starting date : 01/10/2027 \nJob description  \nThe Department of Molecular Biology (DBM) of the Faculty of Sciences at the Université libre de \nBruxelles (ULB) is seeking to recruit a full -time academic staff member to join a multidisciplinary \nresearch and teaching environment. \n \nResearch area \nCandidates with an internationally recognized scientific track record and an innovative research \nprogram in animal developmental biology are encouraged to apply. Priority will be given to candidates \nwhose research activities align with the department's res earch interests and have the potential to \nstrengthen its existing areas of expertise, particularly in the developmental biology of the nervous or \ncardiovascular systems. \n \nThe successful candidate will join the Department of Molecular Biology at the Brussels South Charleroi \nBiopark, a highly dynamic environment dedicated to life sciences: https://biopark.be/en. The Biopark \nhosts three academic research institutes and offers state -of-the-art laboratory facilities, together with \na thriving network of more than 100 companies in the life sciences sector. Within this environment, the \nsuccessful candidate will have opportunities to develop interdisciplinary collaborations with experts in \ncell and developmental biology, nucleic acid biology, microbiology, immunology, virology, and \nparasitology. \n \nTeaching and research responsibilities \nThe successful candidate is expected to demonstrate strong motivation and solid skills in teaching and \nsupervision. They will contribute to teaching activities primarily focused on developmental biology at \nboth Bachelor's and Master's levels, delivering bo th fundamental and specialized courses. Supervision \nof undergraduate and Master's students, as well as postdoctoral researchers, is also expected. \n \nFor candidates who are not proficient in French, a transitional period of up to three years may be \ngranted to learn French and teach in English. By the end of this period, the successful candidate must \nbe able to teach in French. \n \nThe successful candidate will be expected to lead a competitive research program and secure external \nfunding through European and regional funding schemes (e.g., ERC, Wel-RI, FNRS, etc.). \n \n \n \nTeaching duties at the time of appointment: \n• BIOL-F-318 – Histophysiology and Animal Development: 5 ECTS (partim), Bachelor's Year 3, 18 \nhours of lectures, co-lecturer. \n• BIOL-F-320 – Practical Classes in Histopathology and Animal Development : 5 ECTS (partim), \nBachelor's Year 3, 24 hours of practical classes, elective course, course coordinator. \n• S-BIOG-935 – Developmental Biology (corresponding to the two courses listed above, offered at \nthe Charleroi campus): 5 ECTS, Bachelor's Year 3, lectures and practical classes, course \ncoordinator. \n• S-BIOG-914 – Human Embryology: 5 ECTS (partim), Bachelor's Years 1 –2, 12 hours of lectures \nand 8 hours of practical classes, course coordinator. \n• BMOL-F-419 – Neurosciences and Cardiovascular Biology: 5 ECTS (partim), Master's Year 1, 12 \nhours of lectures and seminars, elective course, co-lecturer. \n \nAdditional elective teaching: \n• BMOL-F-4008 – Practical Classes in Molecular Biology : 5 ECTS, Master's Year 1, 48 hours of \npractical classes, elective course. \n \nQualifications required : \nPhD in Biological or Biomedical Sciences, Medicine, Pharmaceutical Sciences, or a related discipline. \nSkills required  \n• You must have at least four years of postdoctoral research experience at the time of appointment. \n• You must demonstrate postdoctoral research experience and an excellent scientific track record. \n• You must have demonstrated the ability to conduct original, high-quality research appropriate to your \ncareer stage. \n• Research mobility outside the institution where you obtained your PhD, either during or after your \ndoctoral studies, will be taken into account when evaluating your application. \n• If you are not fluent in French (C1 level), an adaptation period may be granted. However, you must be \nable to teach in French by the end of the third year following your appointment. \n• Previous teaching experience will be considered an asset. \n \nInterested ? \nFor more information, please contact Prof. Maud Martin (e-mail: maud.martin@ulb.be). \nYour application will consist of a Curriculum Vitae(if you wish, a standard CV can be downloaded from the \nwebsite: https: //www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-scientifiques-cv-type) and \na document completed using the template available at this URL address \n(https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1e-applic-form-acad-tps-plein89-docx).  \nThis template structures your application by including the following elements: \n• an application letter  \n• a 7,000 -character report (4  pages) presenting the applicant’s research activities and a research \nproject, including how these will integrate into ULB’s research teams \n• a teaching dossier including a 7,000 -character report (4 pages) on the applicant's previous teaching \nactivities and a teaching project for the first five years in this position; these must be relevant to the \nfaculty and to the teaching profiles for the programs to which the applicant is to contribute \n• a note about international achievements and projects \n \n• the names and e -mail addresses of five references (with equal gender representation) who may be \ncontacted by those in charge of evaluating applications.   These references should not have conflicts \nof interest because of family or emotional ties. \n \nIncomplete applications or applications that do not use the template provided will not be examined by the \nselection committee. \n \nThe appointment to the academic staff of ULB is made at ”Chargé de Cours” level. As of their \nappointment, members of academic staff are authorised to use the honorary title of ”Professeur”. \nWhere to go to apply? \nClick here: https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2089/?isInternalUser=true \nFor any connection problems or questions about our application, consult our FAQ :  e-recrut-mode-d-\nemploi-candidat-en-_1734942996246-pdf \nN.B.: SAP complies with European and U.S. regulations and, as a result, does not allow access to its \napplication from the following countries/regions: Crimea, Sevastopol, the Donetsk People’s Republic \n(DNR) / Luhansk People’s Republic (LNR), areas not controlled by the Ukrainian government in the \nKherson and Zaporizhzhia regions, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Russia, and Belarus.  \n \nTherefore, candidates applying from these countries – and only from these countries – can submit their \nCV and application to this address: rectrice@ulb.be \n \nEqual opportunities policy \nULB's personnel management policy is geared towards diversity and equal opportunities. \nWe recruit candidates on the basis of their skills, irrespective of age, gender, sexual orientation, origin, \nnationality, beliefs, disability, etc. \nWould you like to be provided with reasonable accommodation in the selection procedure because of a \ndisability, disorder, or illness?  Please contact Marie Botty, the person in charge of diversity aspects for \nthe academic and scientific staff (marie.botty@ulb.be). Be assured of the confidentiality of this \ninformation. \nMore details on the ULB gender and diversity policy are available at https://www.ulb.be/en/about-\nulb/gender-equality-at-ulb.  \n \n \nYou will find all the regulations relating to academic careers on our site at \nhttp://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/9302.pdf": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher-Cancer biology",
      "description": " \n  \n \nPostdoctoral researcher-Cancer biology \nCancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory \n(CEMLab) \n \nPosition \nThe Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB), led by \nPanagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking motivated researchers to undertake a PhD in cancer research. The candidate \nwill focus on a project to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter - and intra-tumor \nheterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical samples. The successful applicant will join the \nULB Faculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. \n \nAbout CEMLab \nCEMLab investigates the cellular and molecular mechanisms driving the metastatic cascade and explores how the \ntumor ecosystem evolves in primary and metastatic organs. Our goal is to develop a comprehensive understanding \nof the molecular mechanisms and cell -cell interactions that favor metastasis and promote tumor outgrowth in \ndistant organs, with emphasis on lifestyle and environmental factors.  \n \nProfile \nWe are seeking motivated candidates with a PhD in biomedical sciences, molecular biology, biochemistry, or a \nrelated field, and a strong background in cancer biology. Experience with mouse models is mandatory , while a \nbackground in melanoma biology is highly desirable. Candidates should have proven laboratory experience in \nmolecular and cellular biology, a strong publication record in peer -reviewed journals, and the ability to work both \nindependently and collaboratively as part of a team. Excellent organizational skill s and strong interpersonal \ncommunication skills, both verbal and written, are essential. \n \nWhat we offer \nWe offer a full -time, two -year funded contract with the possibility of extension, providing a dynamic research \nenvironment that values excellence, professionalism, and teamwork. Successful candidates will be encouraged and \nsupported in applying for nationa l funding opportunities (FNRS, Télévie, FRIA). This position offers the opportunity to \ncollaborate closely with physicians in an interdisciplinary team and includes access to training courses for professional \ndevelopment. Immediate start is available, and the salary will be commensurate with experience, in accordance with \nULB’s pay scale. \n \nWant to join us? \nInterested candidates should send their application via email to Panagiotis Karras at panagiotis.karras@ulb.be, including \na cover letter detailing relevant skills and experiences and a CV for assessment. Name and contact information of two \nreferences. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Early submissions are encouraged as the \nposition is available for immediate start. For additional information do not hesitate to contact us.  \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/9301.pdf": {
      "title": "Full time position for postdoc bioinformatician",
      "description": " \n  \n \nBioinformatician \nFull time position for postdoc bioinformatician \nCancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) \nPosition \nThe Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB), led by Panagiotis \n(Takis) Karras, is seeking for a skilled bioinformatician with experience in single -cell multi-omics. The candidate will focus on \nprojects to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter - and intra-tumor heterogeneity and plasticity \ncombining mouse models and clinical samples. Applicants should demonstrate expertise in programmin g languages (Python \nand/or R) as well as experience working with high-performance computing clusters. The successful applicant will join the ULB \nFaculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. \n \nAbout CEMLab \nCEMLab investigates the cellular and molecular mechanisms driving the metastatic cascade and explores how the tumor \necosystem evolves in primary and metastatic organs. Our goal is to develop a comprehensive understanding of the molecular \nmechanisms and cell-cell interactions that favor metastasis and promote tumor outgrowth in distant organs. \n \nProfile \nWe are seeking for motivated candidates having the following requirements: \n• Received a PhD within 4 years or are about to graduate from a PhD program in Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or a \nrelated field of biology. \n• Have first-authored original publication(s) in high-quality peer-reviewed journals. \n• Experience with high -throughput omics technologies such as  gene expression transcriptomics, proteomics, epigenomics \netc. \n• Demonstrated experience in cancer biology. \n• Proficiency in Python and/or R.  \n• Experience with high-performance computing clusters and single-cell omics data analysis and integration. \n• Ability to proactively manage and drive projects. \n• Collaborate with wet lab scientists to refine and integrate datasets. \n• Strong written and oral communication skills.   \n \nWhat we offer \n• A full-time, 2-year funded contract, with the possibility of extension. \n• Stimulating research environment promoting quality, professionalism, and teamwork. \n• Opportunity to work on a team in close collaboration with physicians. \n• Possibility to attend training courses to learn and implement new bioinformatics pipelines. \n• Immediate incorporation. \n• Flexible working hours and measures to reconcile work, family and personal life. \n• The salary will be commensurate according to experience following ULB’s pay scale. \n \nWant to join us? \nInterested candidates should send their application via email to Panagiotis Karras at panagiotis.karras@ulb.be, including a \ncover letter detailing relevant skills and experiences and a CV for assessment. Applications will be accepted until the position \nis filled. Early submissions are encouraged as the position is available for immediate start. "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/9297.pdf": {
      "title": "PhD Position in mass spectrometry and cancer biology",
      "description": " \n  \n \nPhD Position in mass spectrometry and cancer biology \nFull time position  \nIRIBHM J.E. Dumont \n  \nAbout the laboratory and environment \n \nThe research unit on kinase addiction and BruProMS (ULB/Erasme Mass Spectrometry and \nProteomics Platform) are based at the IRIBHM J.E. Dumont, at the Université Libre de Bruxelles \n(ULB). \nOur laboratory focuses its research on protein kinase biology, proteomics, phosphoproteomics, \nwith a particular expertise in cell cycle kinases (CDK4, Greatwall/MASTL) and their implication \non cancer. The research group is associated with BruProMS, ULB's mass spectrometry and \nproteomics platform, and partner of the BRUXSOMICS project (FEDER Brussels), an inter -\nuniversity ULB-VUB multi-omics platform using mass spectrometry. \n \nPositions summary \nWe are seeking a motivated PhD student to undertake a doctoral project at the interface of \nchemical proteomics, mass spectrometry -based (phospho)proteomics, cell biology, and \nbioinformatics.  \nThe candidate will work on a project aiming at developing the necessary tools to measure kinase \nactivity profiles directly from clinical samples and to build a functional atlas of poorly \ncharacterized kinases , w ith the long -term ambition of enabling precision medicine by \ncorrelating tumor kinase activity with therapeutic response to kinase inhibitors.  \n \nThe successful candidate will: \n• Develop and lead an independent research project aligned with the lab’s focus; \n• Contribute to collaborative data analyses supporting ongoing studies of the Mass Spectrometry \nand Proteomics Platform; \n \nCandidate profile \nThe ideal candidate should hold, or be expecting to receive within 2025 –2026, Master degree in \nbiomedical sciences, biochemistry, cell biology, bio-engineering, or related field.  \nThe following qualifications will be considered: \n• Documented laboratory experience in cell biology and/or molecular biology \n• Interest or prior exposure to mass spectrometry, proteomics, or phosphoproteomics is a \nstrong asset \n3BIO-BioMatter \n \n• Basic knowledge and skills in bioinformatics (R, Python, or Unix) are an advantage \n• A willingness to learn new tools and methodologies and adapt to new challenges \n• Excellent oral and written communication skills in English \n• Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team \n• Strong motivation, intellectual curiosity, and a proactive attitude \n• Previous research contributions leading to a published or submitted study will be considered \na significant advantage \n \nWhat we offer \n• A first year of PhD fellowship starting when the position is filled. \n• A multidisciplinary and technically rich research environment at the interface of \nproteomics, cell biology, chemistry, and bioinformatics \n• Access to state -of-the-art mass spectrometry infrastructure (BruProMS platform, \nBRUXSOMICS) \n• Active support and mentoring for applying to personal fellowship funding (FRIA, FNRS \naspirant mandate, Télévie…) during the PhD \n• Integration within a stimulating scientific network, including the FNRS Thematic \nDoctoral School in Experimental Cancerology (EDT) \n \nHow to apply \nInterested candidates should send their application by e -mail to Prof. Xavier Bisteau at:  \nxavier.bisteau@ulb.be \nThe application should include: \n• A cover letter outlining your motivation and relevant skills \n• A detailed Curriculum Vitae \n• Contact details for two references (names and e-mail addresses) \n \nDeadline \nApplications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Early applications are strongly \nencouraged, as the position is directly available. "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/9280.pdf": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scientist",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \n \nPostdoctoral Scientist \nMolecular mechanisms of metabolic cell dysfunction \nassociated with protein tyrosine phosphatases \nWe offer a full-time position at the Signal Transduction & Metabolism \nLaboratory in Brussels. \nUniversité libre de Bruxelles \n \n \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory (www.stmlaboratoy.com) led by Dr Esteban Gurzov \nis seeking highly motivated post -doctoral researchers to explore the pathophysiological mechanisms \ncontributing to metabolic dysfunction. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine, \ncharacterised by an impressive track record in research excellence. \n \nProject description: \n \nThe project will take advantage of human stem cells , diabetes cell models, mouse models, \npharmacological approaches and human specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms by which \ndysfunctional signalling contributes to the development of obesity, diabetes and liver cancer, and  to \nexplore novel approaches for combating the pathologies. \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides a world leading environment for creative \nscience. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts \nworking together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n• We believe in a strong scientific commitment and reproducible findings to contribute to the \nway of thinking in diabetes research.  \n \n• Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between \nscientists, physicians and the industry.  \n \nProfile \n \n PhD in metabolic disease and/or metabolism \n Experience with mouse handling and experimentation is essential \n Experience in stem cell culture, molecular  biology/genome editing (e.g. qPCR, \nCRISPR/Cas9 and bulk/single cell RNA -Seq), immunohistochemical and/or  \nbiochemical techniques will be advantageous \n Experience with mouse models of diabetes will be advantageous \n Experience with FACS sorting will be advantageous \n The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be \ncapable of both work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English \n High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications + 3 references should be sent directly to esteban.gurzov@ulb.be  \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nDirector, Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversite libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \n \nSalary : Approximately 2500 € after tax. \nDuration: 1 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/9267.pdf": {
      "title": "PHD STUDENT",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \n \nPHD STUDENT \nDATA SCIENCE & AI  \nRADIOPHYSICS AND MRI PHYSICS LABORATORY– UNIVERSITÉ LIBRE DE BRUXELLES \n  \n \nOptimisation of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma treatment through the \napplication of multimodal data and advanced Artificial Intelligence methods \n \nJob description \nWe are seeking a highly motivated candidate with a Master degree in Computer Science, Civil (ideally \nBiomedical) Engineering, Medical Physics, or equivalent, to conduct research in an ambitious Data \nScience project titled: “ Optimisation of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma  treatment through the \napplication of multimodal data and advanced Artificial Intelligence methods”. The proposal will focus \non all aspects of data science; from supporting the creation of structured databases to the \ndevelopment and validation of multi-modal (including imaging) data analysis pipelines using machine- \nand deep learning. The project will be carried out on ULB's ERASME campus (Anderlecht, Brussels) in \nthe Data Science & AI Research Unit of the Institut Jules Bordet (the Belgian reference centre for cancer \ntreatment), in strong collaboration with the Laboratory of Experimental Gastroenterology  and the \nDepartment of Pathology.  \n \nProject description \nPancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) is the most common and aggressive type of pancreatic \ncancer. It arises from the cells lining the ducts of the pancreas and accounts for the vast majority of \npancreatic tumors. In Belgium, PDAC causes nearly 1,700 deaths each year, making it the fourth leading \ncause of cancer-related death. Due to its aggressive nature, late diagnosis, and resistance to therapy, \nPDAC is projected to become the second most deadly cancer by 2030. \nThe overall prognosis for PDAC remains very poor, with fewer than 12% of patients surviving more \nthan five years after diagnosis. This is largely due to the fact that most patients are diagnosed at an \nadvanced stage, when the disease has already spread locally or to distant organs. \nAt HUB, a unique, comprehensive and multimodal database of PDAC samples has been collected and \nfully annotated with clinical and pathological data. In addition, samples from patients enrolled in \nclinical trials are being prospectively obtained. \nThis PhD project will focus on the development of interpretable AI models that integrate multimodal \ndata—including histopathology, radiology, transcriptomics, and clinical variables —from a unique \ncohort of several hundred PDAC patients to identify predictive biomarkers and therapeutic response \nsignatures. By applying the latest AI technology, including large-scale foundation models, the goal is to \n \nuncover latent patterns linked to molecular subtypes, treatment resistance and patient outcomes. The \ncandidate will work closely with clinical and translational collaborators to ensure clinical relevance and \nto build models capable of guiding personalized treatment decisions. This research has the potential \nto transform PDAC care by enabling data -driven stratification strategies and uncovering mechanistic \ninsights into therapy resistance and tumor evolution. \n \nFurther information on the project can be obtained by contacting: Dr. Ir. Jennifer Dhont (ULB / Institut \nJules Bordet) - jennifer.dhont@hubruxelles.be, Senior Data Scientist, Institut Jules Bordet. \n \nProfile \nWe are looking for a highly motivated, pro -active and creative PhD student who can work in  a \nmultidisciplinary environment composed of physicist s, computer scientists, data scientists and  \nphysicians. The candidate must be able to work independently, as well as demonstrate a strong \ncommitment to the team and have good organizational skills to manage the (international and inter-\ndisciplinary) collaborations in this project. The ideal candidate should:  \n• Hold a Master of Science  or Engineering  degree in one of following disciplines: Computer \nScience, Physics, Biomedical Engineering, Medical Physics or equivalent;  \n• Have demonstrated coding skills (Python, MATLAB or other); \n• Show proof of proficiency in English, both in oral and written communication;  \n• Be a team player who can work autonomously and who is able to meet deadlines;  \n• Be willing to spend part of her/his time abroad for research activities and participation in \nworkshops and conferences;  \n• Be willing to step out of their comfort zone by learning concepts outside of their initial scientific \nbackground (medical oncology, data science);  \n- Experience in - or knowledge of - bioinformatics will be viewed as a significant advantage; \n- Experience with a deep learning framework (Tensorflow, PyTorch) is a plus; \n- A good knowledge of data science , medical image analysis or other omics analysis will be \nconsidered as an asset.  \nWhile some flexibility is possible, we expect team members to be on -site at least 80% of the time \nduring the first year to support collaboration and knowledge sharing. \n \nApplication procedure \nThe position is for an initial duration of two years, renewable once (max: 48 months in total). The \nproject will start October 1st 2025. Soon to be graduating master students are welcome to apply \nprovided that they will have graduated before the start of the position. The candidates already in \npossession of a PhD are not eligible. The applicant should provide a motivation letter, curriculum vitae, \na summary of previous research work / master thesis and the name and e -mail addresses of two \nreference persons by e-mail to Dr. Ir. Jennifer Dhont (Jennifer.dhont@hubruxelles.be) by September \n1st 2025 at the latest. Selected candidates will then be interviewed in the following weeks.  "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/8952.pdf": {
      "title": "Position",
      "description": " \n  \n \nPhD student-Cancer biology \n \nCancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) \n \nPosition \nThe Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory  (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles \n(ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking motivated researchers to undertake a PhD in cancer \nresearch. The candidate will focus on a project to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, \nprofile the inter - and intra -tumor heterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical \nsamples. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine  and the Institute Jules Bordet \nwithin the campus. \n \nAbout CEMLab \nCEMLab investigates the cellular and molecular mechanisms driving the metastatic cascade and \nexplores how the tumor ecosystem evolves in primary and metastatic organs. Our goal is to develop a \ncomprehensive understanding of the molecular mechanisms and cell -cell interactions that favor \nmetastasis and promote tumor outgrowth in distant organs. \n \nProfile \nThe applicant must hold an M.Sc.  (or expecting to receive within 2025)  in biomedical sciences, with \nstrong academic performance. Additionally, the applicant should have documented experience in \nlaboratory work, preferably in cancer research or a related field . Excellent oral and written \ncommunication skills in English are essential. The ideal candidate should be capable of working both \nindependently and collaboratively, with demonstrated strong teamwork and interpersonal skills. \nPrevious research contributions  leading to published studies will be considered a significant \nadvantage.  \n \nWhat we offer \nWe offer a full -time, two -year funded contract with the possibility of extension, providing a dynamic \nresearch environment that values excellence, professionalism, and teamwork. Successful candidates will \nbe encouraged and supported in applying for nationa l funding opportunities (FNRS, Télévie, FRIA). This \nposition offers the opportunity to collaborate closely with physicians in an interdisciplinary team and \n \n  \n \nincludes access to training courses for professional development. Immediate start is available, and the \nsalary will be commensurate with experience, in accordance with ULB’s pay scale. \n \nWant to join us? \nInterested candidates are invited to submit their applications via email to Panagiotis Karras  \nat panagiotis.karras@ulb.be. The application should include: \n• A cover letter outlining relevant skills and experiences, \n• A CV for assessment, and \n• Contact details for two references (including names and contact information). \nJoin us in  Brussels, the vibrant heart of Europe! A highly international city, Brussels offers an \nexceptional quality of life and a dynamic environment to thrive in. \nDeadline \nApplications will be accepted until the position is filled. Early submissions are encouraged as the \nposition is available for immediate start. \n \n \nRelevant publications \n \nKarras P , Black J., McGranahan N. and Marine J -C. Genetic versus non -genetic driver mechanisms of \nmetastasis. Nature 629, 543–554 (2024). \nNowosad, A., Marine, J.-C. & Karras, P. Perivascular niches: critical hubs in cancer evolution. Trends Cancer \n(2023). \nKarras, P. et al. A cellular hierarchy in melanoma uncouples growth and metastasis. Nature 610, 190–198 \n(2022). \nX. Li, P. Karras , R. Torres, F. Rambow, J.v .d Oord, J.C. Marine, L. K os. Disseminated Melanoma Cells \nTransdifferentiate into Endothelial Cells in Intravascular Niches at Metastatic Sites. Cell Rep. 31, (2020). \nKarras, P. et al. p62/SQSTM1 Fuels Melanoma Progression by Opposing mRNA Decay of a Selective Set of \nPro-metastatic Factors. Cancer Cell (2019). "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/8942.pdf": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher - Cancer biology",
      "description": " \n  \n \nPostdoctoral researcher - Cancer biology \n \nCancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) \n \nPosition \nThe Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory  (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles \n(ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking talented a postdoc with a recent PhD or MD/PhD \nand experience in Cancer Biology/Biochemistry/Molecular Biology . The candidate will focus on a \nproject to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter- and intra -tumor \nheterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical samples. The successful applicant \nwill join the ULB Faculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. \n \nAbout CEMLab \nCEMLab investigates the cellular and molecular mechanisms driving the metastatic cascade and \nexplores how the tumor ecosystem evolves in primary and metastatic organs. Our goal is to develop a \ncomprehensive understanding of the molecular mechanisms and cell -cell interactions that favor \nmetastasis and promote tumor outgrowth in distant organs. \n \nProfile \nWe are seeking motivated candidates with a PhD in biomedical sciences, molecular biology, \nbiochemistry, or a related field, and a strong background in cancer biology. Experience with mouse \nmodels is mandatory, while a background in melanoma biology is highly desirable. Candidates should \nhave proven laboratory experience in molecular and cellular biology, a strong publication record in \npeer-reviewed journals, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively as part of a team. \nExcellent organizational skills and strong interpersonal communication skills, both verbal and written, \nare essential. \n \nWhat we offer \nWe offer a full-time, 2-year funded contract with the possibility of extension, providing an engaging research \nenvironment that emphasizes quality, professionalism, and teamwork. The position offers the opportunity \nto work closely with physicians in a collaborative team setting and includes access to training courses for \nprofessional development. Immediate incorporation is available, and the salary will be commensurate with \nexperience, following ULB’s pay scale. \n \n  \n \n \nWant to join us? \nInterested candidates should send their application via email to Panagiotis Karras  at \npanagiotis.karras@ulb.be, including a cover letter detailing relevant skills and experiences and a CV \nfor assessment. Name and contact information of two references. \n \nDeadline \nApplications will be accepted until the position is filled. Early submissions are encouraged as the \nposition is available for immediate start. \n \n \n \nRelevant publications \n \nKarras P , Black J., McGranahan  N. and Marine J -C. Genetic versus non -genetic driver mechanisms of \nmetastasis. Nature 629, 543–554 (2024). \nNowosad, A., Marine, J.-C. & Karras, P. Perivascular niches: critical hubs in cancer evolution. Trends Cancer \n(2023). \nKarras, P. et al. A cellular hierarchy in melanoma uncouples growth and metastasis. Nature 610, 190–198 \n(2022). \nX. Li, P. Karras , R. Torres, F. Rambow, J.v .d Oord, J.C. Marine, L. K os. Disseminated Melanoma Cells \nTransdifferentiate into Endothelial Cells in Intravascular Niches at Metastatic Sites. Cell Rep. 31, (2020). \nKarras, P. et al. p62/SQSTM1 Fuels Melanoma Progression by Opposing mRNA Decay of a Selective Set of \nPro-metastatic Factors. Cancer Cell (2019). "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/8892.pdf": {
      "title": "Position",
      "description": " \n  \n \nBioinformatician \n \nCancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) \nPosition \nThe Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles \n(ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking for a skilled bioinformatician with experience in \nsingle-cell multi -omics. The candidate will focus on projects  to better characterize the drivers of \ncancer metastasis, profile the inter - and intra-tumor heterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse \nmodels and clinical samples. Applicants should demonstrate expertise in programming languages \n(Python and/or R ) as well as experience working with high -performance computing clusters. The \nsuccessful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine  and the Institute Jules Bordet within the \ncampus. \n \nAbout CEMLab \nCEMLab investigates the cellular and molecular mechanisms driving the metastatic cascade and \nexplores how the tumor ecosystem evolves in primary and metastatic organs. Our goal is to develop a \ncomprehensive understanding of the molecular mechanisms and cell -cell interactions that favor \nmetastasis and promote tumor outgrowth in distant organs. \n \nProfile \nWe are seeking for motivated candidates having the following requirements: \n• PhD in Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or a related field.  \n*Candidates without a PhD but with demonstrated expertise  in bioinformatics will also be \nconsidered. \n• Experience with high-throughput omics technologies such as gene expression transcriptomics, \nproteomics, epigenomics etc. \n• Proficiency in Python and/or R.  \n• Ability to acquire and process data from sequencing facilities or public resources, work with \n HPCs, run, adapt existing pipelines.  \n• Work independently and collaboratively within a team. \n• Collaborate with wet lab scientists to refine and integrate datasets. \n• Strong written and oral communication skills.  \n• Experience with high-performance computing clusters and single-cell omics data analysis and \nintegration (desirable). \n \n \n  \n \nWhat we offer \n• A full-time, 2-year funded contract, with the possibility of extension. \n• Stimulating research environment promoting quality, professionalism, and teamwork. \n• Opportunity to work on a team in close collaboration with physicians. \n• Possibility to attend training courses to learn and implement new bioinformatics pipelines. \n• Immediate incorporation. \n• Flexible working hours and measures to reconcile work, family and personal life. \n• The salary will be commensurate according to experience following ULB’s pay scale. \n \nWant to join us? \nInterested candidates should send their application via email to Panagiotis Karras  at \npanagiotis.karras@ulb.be, including a cover letter detailing relevant skills and experiences and a CV \nfor assessment.  \n \nDeadline \nApplications will be accepted until the position is filled. Early submissions are encouraged as the \nposition is available for immediate start. \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/8811.pdf": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral position – 10 Months",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \nPost-doctoral position – 10 Months \nInnoviris Funded project – RD3 – PBM and Analytical Platform of the \nFaculty of Pharmacy \nFull-time position at the Analytical Platform of the Faculty of Pharmacy in Brussels. \n \nJob description \n \nThe Analytical Platform of the Faculty of Pharmacy  (ULB, APFP) is an analytical platform providing \nanalytical solutions, especially through chromatography coupled to mass spectrometry. The Platform is \nhosted by the RD3 – Pharmacognosy, Bioanalysis and Drug Discovery research unit (RD3 – PBM) and \ndevelops tools and methods for identifying and quantifying molecules of interest in therapeutics or \nbiomarkers. These methods are part of the proteomic, glycomic, metabolomic, or lipidomic applications. \nIt has its own research projects and contracts and sup ports the research of other ULB and industrial \nlaboratories. \n \nProject description: \nThe research project is called “Plastic-City” and aims at studying the presence of microplastics (MPs) and \nrelated pollutants in the waterways of the Brussels region (BCR). This project is led by the “Vrij \nUniversiteit Brussels” in collaboration with ULB. The research will be carried out by Analytische, Milieu \nen Geochemie (AMGC/VUB) and the APFP (ULB).  \nThe general objective of this project is to estimate the present and future contribution of the BCR as a \nmicroplastic source for waterways and determine what are the ecological impacts associated to this MP \ncontamination. The project is divides in four work packages: \n1. To assess the present-day plastic use in the BCR and their export as MPs to the Zenne and Canal \nwaterways \n2. To identify and quantify pollutants associated to MPs, evaluate their toxicity at cellular level and \nunderstand their interaction with microplastics. \n3. To define plastic use and waste management scenario, apply them to estimate MP emission of \nBCR to its waterways and evaluate the contamination of Brussels waterways with MPs. \n4. To assess the impact of leaching of inorganic and organic contaminants adsorbed on MPs as well \nas those used as additives in polymer processing that can be ingested by aquatic organisms \n \nAs member of APFP, the proposed research position will mainly focus on analytical developments in \nGC and LC-MS(MS), the job will be dedicated to \n• Analytical development in GC and LC-MS(MS) for detecting and quantifying hydrocarbon, \nplasticizers, pesticides… Samples preparation, analysis… (80 %) \n• Sampling of water and microplastics in the waterways of BCR (10 %) \n• Helping in the model development for management scenario (10 %) \n  \n \n  \n \nProfile \n \nPhD in Analytical Chemistry, Pharmacy, Chemistry, Bioengineering, Biology with:  \n \n• Experience in mass spectrometry analysis \n• Experience in GC and LC coupled to mass spectrometry \n• Experience in sample treatment (SPE, liquid/liquid extraction) \n• Experience in environmental chemistry \n• The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be capable of \nboth working independently and collaboratively in a team \n• Excellent organizational and time management skills \n• Excellent skills in spoken and written English.  \n• High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nAt the time of applying and during the last three years (36 months) , the post-doc researcher has been \nat least 12 months abroad. The PhD has been obtained max 5 years ago. \nInterested ? \nApplications with CV and motivation letter + 2 references should be sent directly to \npierre.van.antwerpen@ulb.be  \n \nProf. Dr Pierre Van Antwerpen \nFaculty of Pharmacy - ULB \nRD3- Pharmacognosy, Bioanalysis, Drug Discovery \nand Analytical Platform of the Faculty of Pharmacy \npierre.van.antwerpen@ulb.be \n+3226505263 \n \nDuration: 10 months full time. \nStarting date: 01 November 2024 \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/8479.pdf": {
      "title": "Duration: 48 months (Starting from January 2024)",
      "description": " \n  \n \n   \n \n \n \n  \n \n \n \n \n \nDuration: 48 months (Starting from January 2024) \nFunding: F.R.S.FNRS – PDR \nKeywords: microfluidics, multiphase flow , droplets, mass transfer , emulsification, encapsulation, \nnucleation, crystallization, soft matter \n \nProject \nThe present project aims at using microfluidic batch (in capsules) to study crystallization processes by \n(de)coupling the nucleation and crystal growth steps through control of seeding. We will develop a  \nmicrofluidic system for seeded crystallization in capsules of organic molecules for the fundamental \nunderstanding of the crystallization process, comparing primary (homogeneous or heterogeneous) and \nsecondary nucleation (in -line nuclei generation). Our systematic investigation of the influence of \nhydrodynamics on nucleation and crystal growth in an original, high throughput setup using core-shell \ncapsules will help in the fundamental  understanding of phenomena involved in crystallization (non -\nclassical theories of nucleation).  Model systems under study will be the polymorphs of glycine (as \nprototype of amino acids) and those of piracetam (prototype of racetams). Results of the crystallization \nassays will be expressed in terms of crystal  yield, crystal morphology, particle size distribution, \ncrystallinity, and characterization of polymorphic form. \n \nTransfers, Interfaces and Processes (TIPs) laboratory of the Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB) focuses \non experimental characterization and mathematical modelling of transport phenomena within systems \ncontaining several phases (gas and/or liquid and/or solid), exchanging matter, heat or momentum, \nthrough an interface between these phases, at scales between the micron and the millimetre. The \nresearch carried out revolves mainly around fundamental and/or generic questions. They have direct \napplications in the fields of health, environment, heat transfer technologies and agro -food, chemical, \nmicrotechnology, microfluidics, pharmaceuticals, materials, and space industries.  \n \nIn terms of facility, the microfluidic lab at TIPs comprises a technological platform including a clean \nroom for photolithography,  a 3D laser writer (Nanoscribe) of  submicrometric resolution and a \nfemtoprint device to etch 3D microstructure in glass. These cutting-edge microfabrication equipment’s \nhave been central in designing nozzles for single and double emulsification, having led to the patented \nRaydrop technology that is now valorised by Secoya Technologies, a spin-off company of the lab. This \ntechnology has been indeed shown to be optimal in generating microcapsules for crystallization, as  \n                           PhD position at TIPs lab - Université Libre de Bruxelles \n \n    CRISTACAPS - Crystallization in capsules: \n     Crystallization in capsules under microfluidic control for      \nthe fundamental study of nucleation processes. \n \n \n \n  \n \n   \n \nrecently published in Chemical Communications. The project will be in direct collaboration with the \nproject partner, Professor Johan Wouters, and his team, at the Université de Namur. \n \nProfile  \nApplicants must have completed a Master degree in physics, chemistry, chemical engineering, \nbioengineering, or similar, with basic knowledge in crystallization and willing to carry both \nexperimental and theoretical works.  \n \nApplication \nInterested and highly motivated applicant should forward a cover letter stating why the applicant is \ninterested in this position, a complete CV with 2 academic referees (with address, phone number and \nemails).  \n \nContact \nBenoit Scheid, FNRS Research Director \nTIPs lab – ULB C.P. 165/67 \n50 Av. F. Roosevelt \n1050 Bruxelles \nBELGIUM \nTel: +32 2 650 48 27 \nEmail: Benoit.Scheid@ulb.be \nwebsite: https://bscheid.ulb.ac.be \n \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7997.pdf": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scientist",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \n \nPostdoctoral Scientist \nMolecular mechanisms of  \nobesity-associated liver cancer \nWe offer a full-time position at the Signal Transduction & Metabolism \nLaboratory in Brussels. \nUniversité libre de Bruxelles \n \n \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory (www.stmlaboratoy.com) led by Dr Esteban Gurzov \nis seeking highly motivated post -doctoral researchers to explore the pathophysiological mechanisms \ncontributing to obesity and metabolic liver dysfunction. The successful applicant will join the Laboratoire \nde Gastroentérologie Exp érimental et Endotools /ULB Faculty of Medicine, characterised by an \nimpressive track record in research excellence. \n \nProject description: \n \nThe project will take advantage of human stem cells , diabetes cell models, mouse models, \npharmacological approaches and human specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms by which \ndysfunctional signalling  contributes to the development of obesity, and complications such as liver \ncancer, and to explore novel approaches for combating the pathologies. \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides a world leading environment for creative \nscience. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts \nworking together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n We believe in a strong scientific commitment and  reproducible findings to contribute to the \nway of thinking in diabetes research.  \n \n Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between \nscientists, physicians and the industry.  \n \nProfile \n \n PhD in metabolic disease and/or metabolism \n Experience with mouse handling and experimentation is essential \n Experience in stem cell culture, molecular  biology/genome editing  (e.g. qPCR, \nCRISPR/Cas9 and bulk/single cell RNA-Seq), immunohistochemical and /or \nbiochemical techniques will be advantageous \n Experience with mouse models of diabetes will be advantageous \n Experience with FACS sorting will be advantageous \n The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be \ncapable of both work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English \n High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications + 3 references should be sent directly to Esteban.Gurzov@ulb.be  \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nHead, Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversite libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \n \nSalary : Approximately 2500 € after tax. \nDuration: 1 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7931.pdf": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral fellow molecular biology/immunology",
      "description": "   \n \n  \n \n \n1 \n \n \nPost-doctoral fellow molecular biology/immunology \nULB Center for Research in Immunology (U-CRI)  \n \nThe ULB Center for Research in Immunology (U-CRI) (Belgium) brings together researchers from the ULB \n(Université Libre de Bruxelles) Faculties of Sciences, Medicine and Pharmacy. Its aim is to promote \nfundamental and translational immunology with research axis on molecu lar immunology, pre -clinical \nimmunology, human and translational immunology (https://u-cri.ulb.be/). The team of David Vermijlen \n(https://u-cri.ulb.be/index.php?action=researchGroups&group=10) is looking for a post-doctoral \nfellow. This project is funded by WELBIO (Walloon Excellence in Life Sciences). \nJob description \nWe offer a post-doctoral position embedded in the U-CRI at the Biopark Campus (rue Adrienne Bolland \n8, 6041 Gosselies, Belgium) in the team of David Vermijlen where you will work together with motivated \nPhD students and a research technician . You will have the possibility to independently lead your \nresearch project, but with sufficient guidance and mentoring, and the possibility to learn a wide set of \ncutting-edge technologies. \nDuration: 2 year full time, renewable. \nStarting date: As soon as possible, till a suitable candidate is found \nProject description: \nγδ T cells are the ‘third’ type of lymphocytes, besides αβ T cells and B cells, that can rearrange gene \nsegments at the DNA level in order to generate variable antigen receptors (γδ T cell receptor (TCR), αβ \nTCR, B cell receptor/antibodies).These three cell lineages have been conserved seemingly since the \nemergence of jawed vertebrates, more than 450 million years ago. A main difference with conventional \nαβ T cells is that γδ T cells use their TCR to recognize antigens in a fundamentally different way, i.e. they \ndo not depend on classical MHC molecules. γδ T cells can have several roles, including protection against \ninfections and tumors. \nBased on past and recent findings generated by the ‘David Vermijlen group’ (U -CRI) regarding thymic \ndevelopment and function of γδ T cells (mainly in human), we hypothesize that: \n(i) thymic development of γδ T cells in the human fetus follow unique molecular rules \n(ii) γδ T cells are crucial mediators of anti-microbial immunity in early life \n(iii) γδ T cells generated in the human fetus pers ist and play an important role in anti -cancer \nsurveillance in human tissues in the adult \nWithin this research thematic, the post-doctoral fellow will focus on the understanding of the \nmolecular mechanisms of our observations, especially regarding human γδ T cell development.  \n\n \n2 \n \nProfile \n Ph.D. in biology, bio -engineering sciences, biomedical sciences, pharmaceutical sciences , \nmedical sciences or related disciplines \n Strong expertise in molecular biology /biochemistry (for example RNA -protein interactions, \nimmunoprecipitation, CRISPR-Cas9,…) \n Experience in immunology is beneficial \n Good spoken and written English skills \n \nApplication  \nEnquiries and applications should be made to David Vermijlen at David.Vermijlen@ulb.be. Please email \na CV, motivation letter , summary of past research and recommendation or contact details of two \nreferees. Selection will start in November/December 2022 till a suitable candidate is found. \n \nSelected publications \n Sánchez Sánchez, G., Papadopoulou, M., Azouz, A., Tafesse, Y., Mishra, A., Chan, J. K. Y., Fan, \nY., Verdebout, I., Porco, S., Libert, F., Ginhoux, F., Vandekerckhove, B., Goriely, S., & Vermijlen, \nD. (2022). Identification of distinct functional t hymic programming of fetal and pediatric \nhuman γδ thymocytes via single -cell analysis. Nature communications , 13(1), 5842. \ndoi:10.1038/s41467-022-33488-2 \n Papadopoulou, M., Sánchez Sánchez, G., & Vermijlen, D. (2020). Innate and adaptive γδ T cells: \nHow, when, and why. Immunological Reviews. doi:10.1111/imr.12926 \n Papadopoulou, M., Dimova, T., Shey, M., Briel, L., Veldtsman, H., Khomba, N., Africa, H., Steyn, \nM., Hanekom, W. W., Scriba, T. T., Nemes, E., & Vermijlen, D. (2020). Fetal public Vγ 9Vδ2 T \ncells expand and gain potent cytotoxic functions early after birth. PNAS, 117(31), 18638-18648. \ndoi:10.1073/pnas.1922595117 \n Tieppo, P., Papadopoulou, M., Gatti, D., McGovern, N., Chan, J. K. Y., Gosselin, F., Goetgeluk, \nG., Weening, K., Ma, L., Dauby, N., Cogan, A., Donner, C., Ginhoux, F., Vandekerckhove, B., & \nVermijlen, D. (2020). The human fetal thymus generates invariant effector γδ T cells. The \nJournal of Experimental Medicine, 217(3). doi:10.1084/jem.20190580 \n Dimova, T., Brouwer, M., Gosselin,  F., Tassignon, J., Leo, O., Donner, C., Marchant, A., & \nVermijlen, D. (2015). Effector Vγ9Vδ2 T cells dominate the human fetal γδ T -cell repertoire. \nPNAS, 112(6), E556-E565. doi:10.1073/pnas.1412058112 \n Vermijlen, D., Brouwer, M., Donner, C., Liesnard, C., Tackoen, M., Van Rysselberge, M., Twite, \nN., Goldman, M., Marchant, A., & Willems, F. (2010). Human cytomegalovirus elicits fetal γδ T \ncell responses in utero. The Journal of Experimental Medicine , 207(4), 807 -821. \ndoi:10.1084/jem.20090348 \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7929.pdf": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral fellow molecular biology/immunology",
      "description": "   \n \n  \n \n \n1 \n \n \nPost-doctoral fellow molecular biology/immunology \nULB Center for Research in Immunology (U-CRI)  \n \nThe ULB Center for Research in Immunology (U-CRI) (Belgium) brings together researchers from the ULB \n(Université Libre de Bruxelles) Faculties of Sciences, Medicine and Pharmacy. Its aim is to promote \nfundamental and translational immunology with research axis on molecu lar immunology, pre -clinical \nimmunology, human and translational immunology (https://u-cri.ulb.be/). The team of David Vermijlen \n(https://u-cri.ulb.be/index.php?action=researchGroups&group=10) is looking for a post-doctoral \nfellow. This project is funded by WELBIO (Walloon Excellence in Life Sciences). \nJob description \nWe offer a post-doctoral position embedded in the U-CRI at the Biopark Campus (rue Adrienne Bolland \n8, 6041 Gosselies, Belgium) in the team of David Vermijlen where you will work together with motivated \nPhD students and a research technician . You will have the possibility to independently lead your \nresearch project, but with sufficient guidance and mentoring, and the possibility to learn a wide set of \ncutting-edge technologies. \nDuration: 2 year full time, renewable. \nStarting date: As soon as possible, till a suitable candidate is found \nProject description: \nγδ T cells are the ‘third’ type of lymphocytes, besides αβ T cells and B cells, that can rearrange gene \nsegments at the DNA level in order to generate variable antigen receptors (γδ T cell receptor (TCR), αβ \nTCR, B cell receptor/antibodies).These three cell lineages have been conserved seemingly since the \nemergence of jawed vertebrates, more than 450 million years ago. A main difference with conventional \nαβ T cells is that γδ T cells use their TCR to recognize antigens in a fundamentally different way, i.e. they \ndo not depend on classical MHC molecules. γδ T cells can have several roles, including protection against \ninfections and tumors. \nBased on past and recent findings generated by the ‘David Vermijlen group’ (U -CRI) regarding thymic \ndevelopment and function of γδ T cells (mainly in human), we hypothesize that: \n(i) thymic development of γδ T cells in the human fetus follow unique molecular rules \n(ii) γδ T cells are crucial mediators of anti-microbial immunity in early life \n(iii) γδ T cells generated in the human fetus pers ist and play an important role in anti -cancer \nsurveillance in human tissues in the adult \nWithin this research thematic, the post-doctoral fellow will focus on the understanding of the \nmolecular mechanisms of our observations, especially regarding human γδ T cell development.  \n\n \n2 \n \nProfile \n Ph.D. in biology, bio -engineering sciences, biomedical sciences, pharmaceutical sciences , \nmedical sciences or related disciplines \n Strong expertise in molecular biology /biochemistry (for example RNA -protein interactions, \nimmunoprecipitation, CRISPR-Cas9,…) \n Experience in immunology is beneficial \n Good spoken and written English skills \n \nApplication  \nEnquiries and applications should be made to David Vermijlen at David.Vermijlen@ulb.be. Please email \na CV, motivation letter , summary of past research and recommendation or contact details of two \nreferees. Selection will start in November/December 2022 till a suitable candidate is found. \n \nSelected publications \n Sánchez Sánchez, G., Papadopoulou, M., Azouz, A., Tafesse, Y., Mishra, A., Chan, J. K. Y., Fan, \nY., Verdebout, I., Porco, S., Libert, F., Ginhoux, F., Vandekerckhove, B., Goriely, S., & Vermijlen, \nD. (2022). Identification of distinct functional t hymic programming of fetal and pediatric \nhuman γδ thymocytes via single -cell analysis. Nature communications , 13(1), 5842. \ndoi:10.1038/s41467-022-33488-2 \n Papadopoulou, M., Sánchez Sánchez, G., & Vermijlen, D. (2020). Innate and adaptive γδ T cells: \nHow, when, and why. Immunological Reviews. doi:10.1111/imr.12926 \n Papadopoulou, M., Dimova, T., Shey, M., Briel, L., Veldtsman, H., Khomba, N., Africa, H., Steyn, \nM., Hanekom, W. W., Scriba, T. T., Nemes, E., & Vermijlen, D. (2020). Fetal public Vγ 9Vδ2 T \ncells expand and gain potent cytotoxic functions early after birth. PNAS, 117(31), 18638-18648. \ndoi:10.1073/pnas.1922595117 \n Tieppo, P., Papadopoulou, M., Gatti, D., McGovern, N., Chan, J. K. Y., Gosselin, F., Goetgeluk, \nG., Weening, K., Ma, L., Dauby, N., Cogan, A., Donner, C., Ginhoux, F., Vandekerckhove, B., & \nVermijlen, D. (2020). The human fetal thymus generates invariant effector γδ T cells. The \nJournal of Experimental Medicine, 217(3). doi:10.1084/jem.20190580 \n Dimova, T., Brouwer, M., Gosselin,  F., Tassignon, J., Leo, O., Donner, C., Marchant, A., & \nVermijlen, D. (2015). Effector Vγ9Vδ2 T cells dominate the human fetal γδ T -cell repertoire. \nPNAS, 112(6), E556-E565. doi:10.1073/pnas.1412058112 \n Vermijlen, D., Brouwer, M., Donner, C., Liesnard, C., Tackoen, M., Van Rysselberge, M., Twite, \nN., Goldman, M., Marchant, A., & Willems, F. (2010). Human cytomegalovirus elicits fetal γδ T \ncell responses in utero. The Journal of Experimental Medicine , 207(4), 807 -821. \ndoi:10.1084/jem.20090348 \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7863.pdf": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral position – 3 years",
      "description": " \n  \n \nPost-doctoral position – 3 years \nInnoviris Funded project – RD3 – PBM and Analytical Platform of the \nFaculty of Pharmacy \nFull-time position at the Analytical Platform of the Faculty of Pharmacy in Brussels. \n \nJob description \n \nThe Analytical Platform of the Faculty of Pharmacy  (ULB, APFP) is an analytical platform providing \nanalytical solutions, especially through chromatography coupled to mass spectrometry. The Platform is \nhosted by the RD3 – Pharmacognosy, Bioanalysis and Drug Discovery research unit (RD3 – PBM) and \ndevelops tools and methods for identifying and quantifyin g molecules of interest in therapeutics or \nbiomarkers. These methods are part of the proteomic, glycomic, metabolomic, or lipidomic applications. \nIt has its own research projects and contracts and supports the research of other ULB and industrial \nlaboratories. \n \nProject description: \nThe research project is called “Plastic-City” and aims at studying the presence of microplatics (MPs) and \nrelated pollutants in the waterways of the Brussels region (BCR). This project is led by the “Vrij \nUniversiteit Brussels” in collaboration with ULB. The research will be carried out by Analytische, Milieu \nen Geochemie (AMGC/VUB) and the APFP (ULB).  \nThe general objective of this project is to estimate the present and future contribution of the BCR as a \nmicroplastic source for waterways and determine what are the ecological impacts associated to this MP \ncontamination. The project is divides in four work packages: \n1. To assess the present-day plastic use in the BCR and their export as MPs to the Zenne and Canal \nwaterways \n2. To identify and quantify pollutants associated to MPs, evaluate their toxicity at cellular level and \nunderstand their interaction with microplastics. \n3. To define plastic use and waste management scenario, apply them to estimate MP emission of \nBCR to its waterways and evaluate the contamination of Brussels waterways with MPs. \n4. To assess the impact of leaching of inorganic and organic contaminants adsorbed on MPs as well \nas those used as additives in polymer processing that can be ingested by aquatic organisms \n \nAs member of APFP, the proposed research position will mainly focus on analytical developments in \nGC and LC-MS(MS), the job will be dedicated to \n• Analytical development in GC and LC-MS(MS) for detecting and quantifying hydrocarbon, \nplasticizers, pesticides… Samples preparation, analysis… (80 %) \n• Sampling of water and microplastics in the waterways of BCR (10 %) \n• Helping in the model development for management scenario (10 %) \n  \n \nProfile \n \nPhD in Analytical Chemistry, Pharmacy, Chemistry, Bioengineering, Biology with:  \n \n• Experience in mass spectrometry analysis \n• Experience in GC and LC coupled to mass spectrometry \n• Experience in sample treatment (SPE, liquid/liquid extraction) \n• Experience in environmental chemistry \n• The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be capable of \nboth work independently and collaboratively in a team \n• Excellent organizational and time management skills \n• Excellent skills in spoken and written English.  \n• High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nAt the time of applying  and during the last three years (36 months), the post-doc researcher has been \nat least 12 months abroad. The PhD has been obtained max 5 years ago. \nInterested ? \nApplications with CV and motivation letter + 2 references should be sent directly to \npierre.van.antwerpen@ulb.be  \n \nProf. Dr Pierre Van Antwerpen \nFaculty of Pharmacy - ULB \nRD3- Pharmacognosy, Bioanalysis, Drug Discovery \nand Analytical Platform of the Faculty of Pharmacy \npierre.van.antwerpen@ulb.be \n+3226505263 \n \nDuration: 3-year full time. \nStarting date: 01 September 2022. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7747.pdf": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Lab Organisation",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \n \nResearch Assistant/Lab Organisation \nLaboratory of Signal Transduction and Metabolism \nWe offer a full-time position at the ULB Faculty of Medicine. \n \n \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory (www.stmlaboratoy.com) led by Dr Esteban Gurzov \nis seeking a highly motivated technician/lab manager  to assist researchers to  explore the \npathophysiological mechanisms contributing to the development of metabolic disorders. The successful \napplicant will join the Laboratoire de Gastroentérologie Expérimental et Endotools /ULB Faculty of \nMedicine, characterised by an impressive track record in research excellence. \n \nProject description: \n \nThe project will take advantage of human stem cells, CRISPR/Cas9, diabetes cell models, cell lines and \nhuman specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms which drive the development of metabolic \ndisorders and explore novel approaches for combating obesity, diabetes and liver cancer. \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides a world leading environment for creative \nscience. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts \nworking together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n We believe in a strong scientific commitment and reproducible findings to contribute to the \nway of thinking in diabetes research.  \n \n Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between \nscientists, physicians and the industry.  \nTasks \n Prepare SOPs \n Laboratory organisation \n Mouse colony management \n Safety instructions \n Quality controls \n \n Routine experiments (ELISA, PCR, Stem Cell Culture) \n Learn purchase/ordering using SAP \nProfile \n \n The candidate should have a Master degree  \n Experience in cell culture, molecular biology and biochemical techniques is essential \n Experience with mouse handling and experimentation is essential \n Experience with mouse models of obesity/diabetes will be advantageous \n Experience with stem cell culture will be advantageous \n The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be \ncapable of both work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English \n French knowledge is advantageous \n High motivation and flexibility are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications + 3 references should be sent directly to Esteban.Gurzov@ulb.be  \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nHead, Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversite libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \n \nSalary : Approximately 2100-2400 € after tax. \nDuration: 1 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7733.pdf": {
      "title": "Calling for Expression of Interest (EOI) – Postdoctoral fellowship",
      "description": " \n  \n \nCalling for Expression of Interest (EOI) – Postdoctoral fellowship \n \nChargé de recherches (CR) and Marie-Sklodowska Curie European \nFellowship (MSCA-IF) \nAt the 3BIO-BioMatter unit, the Free University of Brussels (ULB) \n  \nDescription  \nLaboratory of BioMatter  at the faculty of Engineering, the Free University  of Brussels aims to \nidentify potential international candidates interested in the field of biomaterials engineering:  \n \nCandidates with the required profile will work with us to submit a full application to the Marie-\nSklodowska Curie European Fellowship, Chargé de recherches - CR schemes. \n \nThe focus is on design and development of 3D model for soft tissue engineering including \nengineering extracellular matrix to model tumour microenvironment. \n  \nThe broader potential research themes are: \n \nBiomaterials for tissue engineering applications: \n• Hydrogels including enzymatic crosslinking for TE applications \n• 3D models for TE applications \nBiomaterial synthesis and characterisation: \n• Polymeric/Biopolymeric biomaterials \n• Composites and nanocomposites \n• Stimuli-responsive biomaterials \nAdditive Manufacturing/3D Printing: \n• Biomaterials for extrusion printing \n• 3D bioprinting/biofabrication \n• Melt Electro Writing (MEW) \n• Biomaterials (including coatings) for local drug and growth factor delivery \nBiomaterials for specific medical applications: \n• Skin and mucosa \n• Wound healing and tissue adhesives \n \n \n \n\n \nInterested individuals who have clear research topics and can write an excellent proposal under \nour guidance are required to submit an EOI applicat ion form using the links below in the first \ninstance by 25 May 2022. Please note that this is not a funded position bu t an expression of \ninterest to apply for funding. \n \nProject description: \nDuration : 1-3 years depending on the call \nUseful Links  \nThe following links will provide additional informa tion  \nChargé de recherches - CR   \nH2020 guide for applicants  \nScheme Details  \nThe MSCE and CR Fellowships offer individuals the o pportunity to enhance their career \ndevelopment and prospects by spending a period work ing abroad.  The schemes support the \nbest, most promising individual researchers from an ywhere in the world, and any nationality. \nOnly experienced researchers can apply, and this me ans that the applicant must: \n• Hold a Ph. D in chemical engineering, materials sci ence and engineering, biological \nengineering, chemistry, and other relevant fields  \n• Have a research topic(s) and able to write an excel lent proposal under our \nsupervision before the deadlines . \n• An excellent publication track record.\nAnd be able to satisfy most of the following requir ements \n(1) Biomaterials, e.g., hydrogel and scaffold desig n, synthesis, and characterization \n(2) Invitro techniques such as cell culture models,  cytotoxicity tests, \nimmunohistochemistry, and protein and gene expressi on analyses \n(3) Bioprinting techniques, such as micro-extrusion , DLP, etc. \n(4) In vivo models, imaging, and tissue evaluation \n \nApplication Process & Deadlines  \nExpressions of Interest must be submitted using the  APPLICATION FORM , together with a \nfull CV (no more than three pages), by email to amin.shavandi@ulb.be  no later than 25 May \n2022. Only applicants who provide a clear, focused, and detailed  outline of their proposed \nresearch can expect a response by the 10 th  of June 2022. \nAll required documents should be combined in the fo rm of one single pdf file and no larger \nthan 500 KB.  \nThe subject of the email: EOI – FIRST NAME, LAST NA ME \n \nQuestions \nFor any queries relating to this call, please direc t these to Amin Shavandi \n(amin.shavandi@ulb.be ). \n \n \n \n \n \n3BIO-BioMatter \n \n \n \n \nApplicant information \n Name of applicant  \n Email address  \n Current position and institution  \n \n \nProposed research \n Title of the proposal: \n \n Please give a brief and detailed outline of the nature of your proposed research, including its \naims and objectives in detail (no more than 500 words). \n \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7630.pdf": {
      "title": "WE OFFER A FULL-TIME POSITION AT THE SOLVAY BRUSSELS SCHOOL OF",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \nDoctoral student in Supply Chain Management \nWE OFFER A FULL-TIME POSITION AT THE SOLVAY BRUSSELS SCHOOL OF \nECONOMICS AND MANAGEMENT \n \n \nJob description \nThe Solvay Brussels School of Economics and Management (ULB) has currently a phd position available \nin the area of supply chain management. The overall topic of the PhD is risk management in covid-\ntimes, linked to supply chain management and operations management. The PhD track enables a fast \ntrack PhD as there are limited teaching obligations in the first two-years (there is already full-time \nfunding for the first two years) based on an FNRS funding. The PhD is guided by Professor Dr. Evelyne \nVanpoucke. The successful applicant will join the SBS-EM, characterised by a remarkable track record in \nresearch excellence. \n \nDoctoral program \nOur school consists of a vibrant mix of people interested in economics and management. We actively \nstrive to create and maintain an intellectually stimulating environment, advancing the scientific \nknowledge in the areas mentioned above, while at the same time contributing to the development of \neffective practices for companies, organizations and society. Our school is highly recognized, both \nnationally and internationally. \n \nThe Ph.D. studies also involve advanced training (in French: “formation doctorale”) that helps Ph.D. \ncandidates acquire the necessary tools and knowledge to carry out independent research. At SBS-EM, \nthis training is organised in “tracks”, which correspond to different areas of specialisation: \nManagement Science, Economics and Economics & Statistics. Each track has its own requirements. \nTracks are hosted in research centers, which also provide administrative and logistical support for their \ndoctoral students. As of today, about 100 doctoral students are enrolled at SBS-EM. SBS-EM is part of \nthe Graduate School in Economics (all universities in French-speaking Belgium + KU Leuven) and the \nEcole Doctorale Thématique en Sciences de Gestion (ULB - U. Mons – HEC Liège) which pool the offer \nof advanced courses across the member universities. All registered Ph.D. students at SBS-EM have \naccess to these courses.\n \nProfile \nRequired Qualifications and skills for the position: \n- Master Degree in Management/business engineering or related field (a two-year master degree) with \ngraduation date in the last three years \n   \n \n- a clear interest in supply chain /operations management  \n- outstanding academic performance \n- a research mind-set and good analytical skills \n- Interested in research relevant to both the academic and the business world \n- Have good writing skills and fluent in English \n- a pro-active attitude \n \nInterested ? \nPlease send your letter of intent, curriculum vitae (including publication list), and the name of 2-3 \nreference persons (with email address and telephone number) to Evelyne.vanpoucke@ulb.be. Don’t \nhesitate to contact me if you need more info. The vacancy is open till the 15th of June 2022, but early \napplications are encouraged, as the position is already open at the moment. \n \nEvelyne Vanpoucke  \nAvenue F. Roosevelt 42 \n1050 Brussels \n \nDuration: 2 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: 2022 \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7629.pdf": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral position in Supply Chain Management",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \nPost-doctoral position in Supply Chain Management \nWE OFFER A FULL-TIME POSITION AT THE SOLVAY BRUSSELS SCHOOL OF \nECONOMICS AND MANAGEMENT \n \n \nJob description \nThe Solvay Brussels School of Economics and Management (ULB) has currently a post-doctoral position \navailable in the area of supply chain management. The overall topic of the post-doctoral position is risk \nmanagement in covid-times, linked to supply chain management and operations management. The \nPhD track enables a fast track PhD as there are limited teaching obligations in the first two-years (there \nis already full-time funding for the first two years) based on an FNRS funding. The PhD is guided by \nProfessor Dr. Evelyne Vanpoucke. The successful applicant will join the SBS-EM, characterised by a \nremarkable track record in research excellence. \n \nDoctoral program \nOur school consists of a vibrant mix of people interested in economics and management. We actively \nstrive to create and maintain an intellectually stimulating environment, advancing the scientific \nknowledge in the areas mentioned above, while at the same time contributing to the development of \neffective practices for companies, organizations and society. Our school is highly recognized, both \nnationally and internationally. \n \nThe post-doctoral position is financed by MIS FNRS funding (a scientific funding) for a period of 2 years. \nThe research project will be about risk management in supply chains and will be guided by Professor \nEvelyne Vanpoucke. The post-doctoral position will also be involved in guiding a Ph.D. student on this \ntopic. \n \nProfile \nRequired Qualifications and skills for the position: \n- PhD in Management, industrial engineering, economics or related field with graduation date in the last \nfive years \n- a clear interest in supply chain /operations management  \n- outstanding academic performance \n- a research mind-set and good analytical skills \n- Interested in research relevant to both the academic and the business world \n- Have good writing skills and fluent in English \n- a pro-active attitude \n   \n \nInterested ? \n \nPlease send your letter of intent, curriculum vitae (including publication list), and the name of 2-3 \nreference persons (with email address and telephone number) to Evelyne.vanpoucke@ulb.be. Don’t \nhesitate to contact me if you need more info. The vacancy is open till the 15th of June 2022, but early \napplications are encouraged, as the position is already open at the moment. \n \nEvelyne Vanpoucke  \nAvenue F. Roosevelt 42 \n1050 Brussels \n \nDuration: 2 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: 2022 \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7539.pdf": {
      "title": "Technician",
      "description": " \n  \n \nTechnician \nERC Funded project - Laboratory of Signal Transduction and \nMetabolism \nFull-time position at the Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory in Brussels. \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory (www.stmlaboratoy.com) led by Dr Esteban Gurzov \nis seeking a highly motivated technician to assist researchers to  explore the pathophysiological \nmechanisms contributing to the development of metabolic disorders. The successful applicant will join \nthe Laboratoire de Gastroentérologie Expérimental et Endotools/ULB Faculty of Medicine, characterised \nby an impressive track record in research excellence. \n \nProject description: \nThe project will take advantage of human stem cells, CRISPR/Cas9, diabetes cell models, cell lines and \nhuman specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms which drive the development of metabolic \ndisorders and explore novel approaches for combating obesity, diabetes and liver cancer. \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides a world leading environment for creative \nscience. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts \nworking together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n We believe in a strong scientific commitment and reproducible findings to contribute to the way \nof thinking in diabetes research.  \n \n Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between \nscientists, physicians and the industry.  \n \nProfile \n \n Experience in stem cell culture and biochemical techniques is essential \n Experience with CRISPR gene editing will be advantageous \n Experience with staff management will be advantageous \n The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be capable of \nboth work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English.  \n High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications + 3 references should be sent directly to Esteban.Gurzov@ulb.be  \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nHead, Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversite libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \n \nSalary : Approximately 2100-2400 €/month. \nDuration: 1 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7538.pdf": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scientist",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \nPostdoctoral Scientist \nMolecular mechanisms of Metabolic Diseases  \nFull-time position at the Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory in Brussels \n \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory (www.stmlaboratoy.com) led by Dr Esteban Gurzov \nis seeking highly motivated post -doctoral researchers to explore the pathophysiological mechanisms \ncontributing to obesity, diabetes, and metabolic liver dysfunction. The successful applicant will join the \nLaboratoire de Gastroentérologie Expérimental et Endotools/ULB Faculty of Medicine, characterised by \nan impressive track record in research excellence. \n \n \nProject description: \nThe project will take advantage of human stem cells , diabetes cell models, mouse models, \npharmacological approaches and human specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms by which \ndysfunctional signalling contributes to the development of obesity, diabetes and complications such as \nliver cancer, and to explore novel approaches for combating the pathologies. \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides a world leading environment for creative \nscience. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts \nworking together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n We believe in a strong scientific commitment and reproducible findings to contribute to the way \nof thinking in diabetes research.  \n \n Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between \nscientists, physicians and the industry.  \nProfile \n \n PhD in metabolic disease and/or metabolism \n Experience with mouse handling and experimentation is essential \n Experience in stem cell culture, molecular biology/genome editing (e.g. qPCR, CRISPR/Cas9 and \nbulk/single cell RNA-Seq), immunohistochemical and /or biochemical techniques will be \nadvantageous \n Experience with mouse models of diabetes will be advantageous \n Experience with FACS sorting will be advantageous \n \n The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be capable of \nboth work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English \n High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications + 3 references should be sent directly to Esteban.Gurzov@ulb.be  \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nHead, Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversite libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \n \nSalary : Approximately 2500 € after tax. \nDuration: 1 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7422.pdf": {
      "title": "PhD Student Full-time position",
      "description": " \n  \n \nPhD Student Full-time position \nTELEVIE Funded project \nLiver inflammation and cancer in obesity \nat the Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory  (www.stmlaboratory.com) led by Dr Esteban Gurzov is \nseeking highly motivated PhD students  to explore the pathophysiological mechanisms contributing to the \ndevelopment of obesity and liver dysfunction . The successful applicant will join the Laboratoire de \nGastroentérologie Expérimental et Endotools /ULB Faculty of Medicine, characterised by an impressive track \nrecord in research excellence. \n \nProject description: \n \nThe project will take a dvantage of human stem cells , hepatic cancer cell models, mouse models, \npharmacological approaches and human liver specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms by which \nobesity drives the development of hepatocellular carcinoma  and explore novel approaches for  \ncombating the disease.  \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory  provides an international and world leading environment \nfor creative science. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts \nworking together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n We believe in a strong scientific commitment and reproducible findings to contribute to the way of \nthinking in metabolic research.  \n Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between scientists, \nphysicians and the industry.   \n \nProfile \n \n Experience in cell culture, molecular biology/genome editing (e.g. qPCR, CRISPR/Cas9 and RNA -Seq), \nimmunohistochemical and biochemical techniques will be advantageous \n Experience with mouse handling and experimentation will be advantageous \n Experience with mouse models of obesity/cancer/liver dysfunction will be advantageous \n Experience with stem cell culture and/or mass spectrometry will be advantageous \n The candidate should be capable of both work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English \n High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications should be sent directly to esteban.gurzov@ulb.ac.be \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nHead, Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversité libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \n \n \nStarting date: January 2022. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7401.pdf": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scientist",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \n Postdoctoral Scientist \nJDRF funded project - Molecular mechanisms of autoimmune diabetes \nWe offer a full-time position at the Signal Transduction  \n& Metabolism Laboratory in Brussels. \nUniversité libre de Bruxelles \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory led by Dr Esteban Gurzov is seeking highly \nmotivated post-doctoral researchers to develop novel methods to diagnose type 1  diabetes, and to \nexplore the pathophysiological mechanisms contributing to autoimmune diabetes. The successful \napplicant will join the Laboratoire de Gastroentérologie Expérimental et Endotools /ULB Faculty of \nMedicine (www.stmlaboratoy.com), characterised by an impressive track record in research excellence. \n \nProject description: \n \nThe project will take advantage of human iPSC, diabetes cell models, mouse models, pharmacological \napproaches and human specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms by which tyrosine \nphosphatases contribute to the development of autoimmune diabetes and to explore novel approaches \nfor combating type 1 diabetes. \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides a world leading environment for creative \nscience. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts \nworking together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n We believe in a strong scientific commitment and  reproducible findings to contribute to the \nway of thinking in diabetes research.  \n \n Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between \nscientists, physicians and the industry.  \nProfile \n \n PhD in autoimmune disease and/or metabolism \n Experience with mouse handling and experimentation is essential \n Experience in cell culture, molecular  biology/genome editing  (e.g. qPCR, \nCRISPR/Cas9 and RNA-Seq), immunohistochemical and/or biochemical techniques is \nessential \n \n Experience with mouse models of diabetes will be advantageous \n Experience with FACS will be advantageous \n The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be \ncapable of both work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English \n High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications + 3 references should be sent directly to Esteban.Gurzov@ulb.be  \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nHead, Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversite libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \nFax: +32 2 555 6239 \n \nSalary : Approximately 2500 € after tax. \nDuration: 1 year full time in the first instance. \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7336.pdf": {
      "title": "FULL-TIME POSTDOCTORAL SCIENTIST POSITION",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \nFULL-TIME POSTDOCTORAL SCIENTIST POSITION \nERC Funded project \nBioinformatician for obesity-associated liver cancer \nSIGNAL TRANSDUCTION & METABOLISM LABORATORY – UNIVERSITÉ LIBRE DE BRUXELLES \n \n \nJob description \n \nThe Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory led by Dr Esteban Gurzov is seeking highly motivated \npost-doctoral researchers to explore the pathophysiological mechanisms contributing to the \ndevelopment of obesity and hepatocellular carcinoma. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty \nof Medic ine (www.stmlaboratoy.com), characterised by an impressive track record in research \nexcellence. \n \nProject description: \n \nProtein tyrosine phosphatases (PTPs) constitute a superfamily of enzymes that dephosphorylate tyrosine-\nphosphorylated proteins to oppose the actions of protein tyrosine kinases. Our previous studies and \npreliminary data suggest that PTPs act as molecular switches for key signalling events in the development \nof metabolic disorders. \n \nA post-doctoral position is available to fully characterise the activity of key PTPs in metabolic relevant cells \nin obesity and liver cancer. Importantly, these functions of PTPs make them promising drug candidates \nfor the treatment of metabolic disorders. Thus, our work will provide molecular mechanisms to propose \nnovel pre-clinical approaches to treat these pathologies. He/she will use bioinformatics analysis, gene \nediting, single cell RNA-Seq, molecular biology and in vitro and in vivo approaches. \n \n \nThe Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides an international and world leading \nenvironment for creative science. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic \ndiseases, with experts working together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! \n \n We believe in a strong scientific commitment and reproducible findings to contribute to the \nway of thinking in metabolic research.  \n \n Our vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between \nscientists, physicians and the industry.  \n \nProfile \n \n A PhD in relevant areas and experience in bioinformatics is essential. \n Laboratory experience in metabolism and/or cancer, animal handling and dissection, and \nexperience in molecular/genomic/biochemical techniques will be advantageous. \n Experience with stem cell culture and/or mass spectrometry will be advantageous \n The candidate should have demonstrable track record of research excellence and be capable of \nboth work independently and collaboratively in a team \n Excellent organizational and time management skills \n Excellent skills in spoken and written English \n High motivation, flexibility as well as innovate and creative thinking are a must \n \nInterested ? \n \nApplications should be sent directly to esteban.gurzov@ulb.be \n \nEsteban N. Gurzov, PhD \nHead, Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory \nUniversité libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \n808 Route de Lennik \nB-1070 Brussels \nBelgium \n \nTel: +32 2 555 8908 \n \n \nSalary : Approximately 2400 € after tax. \nDuration: 1 year full time (renewable) \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/greffe/modules/vac/data/sources/pdf/prod/7085.pdf": {
      "title": "Project Description",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \nProject Description \n \nWe are seeking highly motivated post -doctoral researchers to  develop 3D-bioprinted salivary \ngland model to decipher the physiopathology of diseases. PhD candidates will perform their \nresearch in an intellectually stimulating  and multi -disciplinary environment.  The successful \napplicant will join the ULB Laboratory o f Pathophysiological and Nutritional Biochemistry \n(LPNB) (http://lpnb.ulb.be/HOME-PAGE-LPNB.html) and the BioMatter unit  \n(http://biomatter.ulb.be/)    \n \nProfile  \nThe applicant should have a Master and a PhD thesis in the field of medicine, biological sciences, \nchemical engineering or biological engineering. We are looking for a highly motivated person \nwith strong background in molecular biology, biochemistry, biom aterial synthesis,  tissue \nengineering and cell biology who should be able to satisfy most of the following requirements.  \nSpecific Requirements \nCandidates can be EU or Non-EU citizens.  The Candidate have the opportunity to travel \noverseas to ensure technology transfer.   Candidates must have spent one year outside \nBelgium in the past three years. \nExpertise and technical skills: \n Stem cells & regenerative medicine. \n Advanced cell-culture and tissue engineering techniques (e.g., organoids, 3D \nbioprinting, etc.). \n Bioprinting techniques, such as extrusion,  and DLP. \n Biomaterials, e.g., hydrogel and scaffold design, synthesis and characterization \n Immuno-histo/-cyto chemistry, confocal microscopy, flow cytometry/FACS, and \nRNAseq, cell live / death assays. \n In vivo models, imaging, and tissue evaluation \n Preparation of bioactive compounds and hydrogels. \n Physicochemical techniques including SEM, FTIR, rheology. \nFull time Post-Doctoral position in 3D cell bioprinting \n \nAt the Laboratory of Pathophysiological and Nutritional Biochemistry (LPNB) \nand the BioMatter unit, the Free University of Brussels (ULB) \n \n \n \n \nInterested?  \nThe applicant should prepare a unique PDF file containing the following documents in the \nspecified order: \n- cover letter (1 page maximum) \n- curriculum vitae \n- publication list \n- brief overview of relevant experience (1 page maximum)  \n- academic transcripts \nSubmit application to: christine.delporte@ulb.be and amin.shavandi@ulb.be If judged \nsuitable, applicants will be selected for an online interview. \n \nSalary: Approximately 2400 € after tax \nDuration: 2 years full time. \nStarting date: As soon as possible. \n \nDeadline for the submission of applications: Positions open until filled. \n \n \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20496": {
      "title": "POSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN APPRENTISSAGE EN PROFONDEUR, MODÈLES FONDAMENTAUX ET REPRÉSENTATION DES CONNAISSANCES",
      "description": " \n  \nSOUS RESERVE DE L’APPROBATION DU CONSEIL ACADEMIQUE DU 23 NOVEMBRE 2026 \n \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PLEIN EN APPRENTISSAGE EN PROFONDEUR, \nMODÈLES FONDAMENTAUX ET REPRÉSENTATION DES CONNAISSANCES \nFACULTE DES SCIENCES \n \nRéférence : 2027/A021 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures :  15/01/2027 à midi \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 01/10/2027 \nDescriptif du poste \nLe département d'Informatique de la Faculté des Sciences de l'Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \nrecrute un·e académique à temps plein  en intelligence artificielle et apprentissage automatique, \nspécialisé(e) dans les domaines suivants  : apprentissage profond, apprentissage de représentations, \nreprésentation des connaissances, modèles de fondation, modèles du monde et/ou systèmes de \nraisonnement. Le/la candidat.e retenu.e  contribuera à l'enseignement, à la recherche, au \ndéveloppement des programmes et au leadership académique dans un domaine en pleine expansion \nqui redéfinit l'informatique et les disciplines connexes. La prise de fonction est prévue le 1er octobre \n2027. \nLe poste comprend des activités d'enseignement (niveaux Bachelier et Master), de recherche et des \ntâches administratives. Le/la candidat.e idéal.e sera capable d'enseigner des cours allant de \nl'informatique de base  en Bachelier à des cours de Master portant sur des sujets avancés liés à \nl'apprentissage profond, l'apprentissage de représentations, la représentation des connaissances, les \nmodèles de fondation, les modèles du monde et/ou le raisonnement en IA. \nLe département d'Informatique de l'ULB intervient dans différents programmes d'enseignement \nuniversitaires, à Bruxelles et à Charleroi. Les cours de Bachelier sont dispensés en français, tandis que \nles programmes de Master sont tous en anglais. Les candidats ne maîtrisant pas le français bénéficieront \nd'une période d'adaptation, mais devront être en mesure d'enseigner en français à l'issue de la troisième \nannée suivant leur prise de fonction. \nAfin de lutter contre la sous-représentation des femmes dans les disciplines STEM, l’Université veillera \nà respecter une proportion de minimum 30% de femmes avec les qualifications requises dans la short-\nlist et, à compétences égales, la nomination d’une femme. \n \nDomaine de recherche : Sujets liés à l'apprentissage profond, à l'apprentissage de représentations, à la \nreprésentation des connaissances, aux modèles de fondation, aux modèles du monde et/ou aux \nsystèmes de raisonnement avancés \n \nTitre requis  \nDoctorat en informatique, intelligence artificielle, apprentissage automatique ou domaine équivalent.\n \n   \n \nCompétences requises \n• Solide expérience en matière de publications et de recherche, adaptée au niveau de carrière. \n• Le/la candidat.e doit posséder les compétences nécessaires pour enseigner l'informatique aux \nniveaux de Bachelier et Master.  \n• Une expérience postdoctorale et/ou d'enseignement sera appréciée.  \n• Une expérience de recherche en milieu industriel est également reconnue. \n• Une expérience préalable en encadrement d'étudiant .e.s en doctorat et en master, en obtention \nde financements de recherche, ainsi qu'en gestion et direction d'une équipe de recherche sont \nconsidérées comme des atouts. \n• Si vous avez effectué une mobilité en dehors de l’institution où a été réalisé votre doctorat (durant \nla période doctorale ou après), ce sera pris en compte lors de l’évaluation de votre dossier. \n• Si vous ne parlez pas couramment la langue française , une période d’adaptation peut vous être \naccordée, mais vous devrez être capable d’enseigner en français à la fin de la troisième année \nsuivant votre nomination. \n• De bonnes compétences en anglais sont également reconnues comme un atout pour \nl'enseignement dans le programme de master. \nIntéressé·e ? \nPour plus d'informations, veuillez contacter M. Gwenaël Joret (email  : Gwenael.Joret@ulb.be), \nprésident du département d'informatique. \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (si vous le souhaitez un CV type peut \nêtre téléchargé via le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-\net-scientifiques-cv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse \nURL https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1f-dossier-de-candidature-acad-tps-plein-docx).  \n \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants :  \n \n• une lettre de motivation  (avec la possibilité de mentionner les congés de maternité à prendre en \ncompte). \n• un rapport (maximum 6 pages) présentant les activités de recherche de la personne candidate et un \nprojet de recherche, y compris la manière dont celles -ci se développeront en une activité à l’ULB. \nInclure une section mettant en évidence ce que vous considérez comme vos meilleures réalisations. \n• un dossier pédagogique, comprenant un rapport (maximum 4 pages) sur les activités \nd’enseignement antérieures de la personne candidate, et un projet d’enseignement pour les cinq \npremières années du mandat ; ces éléments doivent être pertinents pour la faculté  et les profils \nd’enseignement des programmes auxquels le·la candidat·e contribuera. \n• un énoncé sur la diversité et l’inclusion (expériences passées ou idées pour des initiatives futures). \n• les noms et adresses mail de contact de cinq personnes de référence susceptibles d’être contactées \npar les organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des genres.  Ces personnes ne \npeuvent être en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou affectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \n \nLa nomination, dans le cadre académique de I’ULB, se fait au rang de chargé de cours.  Dès leur \nnomination, les membres du corps académique sont autorisé·e·s à porter, à titre honorifique, le \nqualificatif de professeur·e. \n \n   \n \nLes pages Web suivantes peuvent également être consultées pour plus d'information : \n• https://sciences.ulb.be/en/computer-sciences (Département d’Informatique) \n• http://mlg.ulb.ac.be (le ULB Machine Learning Group) \n \nOù se rendre pour postuler ? \nCliquez ici :  https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2101/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nPour tout problème de connexion ou question à propos de notre application, consultez notre FAQ  : e-\nrecrut-mode-d-emploi-candidat-fr-_1734942952302-pdf \nN.B. : SAP respecte des directives européennes et états-uniennes, et en conséquence, n’autorise pas \nles accès à son application à partir des pays/ régions suivants : La Crimée, Sébastopol, République \npopulaire de Donetsk (DNR) / République populaire de Louhansk (LNR), Les zones non contrôlées par \nle gouvernement ukrainien dans les oblasts de Kherson et Zaporijia, Cuba, l’Iran, La Corée du Nord, la \nSyrie, la Russie et la Biélorussie. \nDès lors, les candidats qui postulent au départ de ces pays – et uniquement au départ de ces pays – \npeuvent envoyer leur curriculum vitae et leur dossier de candidature à cette adresse : rectrice@ulb.be \n \nPolitique d’égalité des chances \nLa politique de gestion du personnel de l’ULB est axée sur la diversité et l’égalité des chances. \nNous recrutons les candidat·es  en fonction de leurs compétences, indépendamment de leur âge, leur \ngenre, leur orientation sexuelle, leur origine, leur nationalité, leurs convictions, leur handicap, etc. \nVous souhaitez bénéficier d’aménagements raisonnables dans le cadre de la procédure de sélection en \nraison d’un handicap, d’un trouble ou d’une maladie ? N’hésitez pas à prendre contact avec Marie Botty \n(marie.botty@ulb.be) notre personne de contact en charge des aspects de diversité pour le personnel \nenseignant et scientifique. Soyez assuré·e de la confidentialité de cette information. \nPlus de détails sur les politiques de genre et de diversité sont disponibles sur https://www.ulb.be/fr/l-\nulb-s-engage/diversites.  \n \n \nVous trouverez l’ensemble des dispositions relatives aux carrières du corps académique sur notre site à \nl’adresse http://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20497": {
      "title": "FULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN DEEP LEARNING, FOUNDATION MODELS AND KNOWLEDGE REPRESENTATION",
      "description": " \n  \nSUBJECT TO THE APPROVAL BY THE ACADEMIC BOARD OF NOVEMBER 23TH, 2026 \n  \nFULL-TIME ACADEMIC POSITION IN DEEP LEARNING, FOUNDATION \nMODELS AND KNOWLEDGE REPRESENTATION \n \nFACULTY OF SCIENCES \n \n \nReference : 2027/A021 \nApplication deadline: 15/01/2027 12:00 PM \nStart date: 01/10/2027  \nJob description  \nThe Computer Science department of the Faculty of Sciences at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB) \ninvites applications for a full -time academic position in artificial intelligence and machine learning, with a \nfocus on topics related to deep learning, r epresentation learning, knowledge representation, foundation \nmodels, world models and/or reasoning systems. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching, \nresearch, curriculum development, and academic leadership in a rapidly evolving field that is reshaping \ncomputer science and related disciplines. The position starts October 1, 2027.   \nThe position involves teaching (at the bachelor and master level), research, and administrative tasks. The \nideal candidate has the capacity to teach courses ranging from classic Computer Science in the bachelor to \nthose explaining advanced topics related to deep learning, representation learning, knowledge \nrepresentation, foundation models, world models and/or AI reasoning in the masters.   \nThe ULB computer science department is involved in different teaching programs in the university, both in \nBrussels and Charleroi. While the bachelor courses are taught in French, the master programs are all in \nEnglish. Applicants who do not speak French will be granted a period of adaptation, but they must be able \nto teach in French at the end of the third year following their appointment. \nULB is strongly committed to improving gender equality.   To combat the under-representation of women \nin STEM disciplines, the University ensure s that a minimum of 30% of women with the required \nqualifications are on the shortlist and, for equal competence, the appointment of a woman  \n \nArea of Research:  Topics related to deep learning, representation learning, knowledge representation, \nfoundation models, world models and/or advanced reasoning systems \n \nQualifications required \nPhD degree in computer science, AI, machine learning or equivalent area.  \nSkills required  \n• A strong publication and research record, appropriate to the career stage. \n• Candidates should have the background to teach computer science courses at both the bachelor \nand the master level. \n \n• Post-doctoral and teaching experience will be appreciated. \n• Research experience within industry is also recognised. \n• Prior expertise in PhD and Master student supervision, attracting research funding, managing and \nleading a research group are all considered assets.   \n• Exchange periods of any duration outside of the applicant’s home institution (during or after their \nPhD) will be taken into consideration when evaluating applications. \n• Applicants who do not speak French may be granted a period of adaptation, but they must be able \nto teach in French at the end of the third year following their appointment. \n• Good English language skills are also recognised as an asset for teaching in the Master program. \n \nInterested ? \nFor more information, please contact Mr. Gwenaël Joret  (E-mail Gwenael.Joret@ulb.be), Head of the \nComputer Science Department. \n \nYour application will consist of a Curriculum Vitae (if you wish, a standard CV can be downloaded from the \nwebsite: https: //www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-scientifiques-cv-type) and \na document completed using the template available at this URL address  \nhttps://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/1e-applic-form-acad-tps-plein-docx.  \n \nThis template structures your application by including the following elements: \n• an application letter (with the possibility of mentioning maternity leaves to be taken into account) \n• a report (maximum 6 pages) presenting the applicant’s research activities and a research project, \nincluding how these will develop into an activity at ULB. Include a section highlighting what you \nconsider to be your best achievements.  \n• a teaching dossier including a report (maximum 4 pages) on the applicant's previous teaching activities \nand a teaching project for the first five years in this position; these must be relevant to the faculty and \nto the teaching profiles for the programmes to which the applicant is to contribute \n• a statement about diversity and inclusion (past experiences or ideas for future initiatives), \n• the names and e-mail addresses of five referees (respecting the gender balance) who may be contacted \nby those in charge of evaluating applications.  These referees should not have conflicts of interest \nbecause of family or emotional ties. \n \nIncomplete applications or applications that do not use the template provided will not be examined by the \nselection committee. \n \nThe appointment to the academic staff of ULB is made at ”Chargé de Cours” level. As of their appointment, \nmembers of academic staff are authorised to use the honorary title of ”Professeur”. \nThe following web pages can also be consulted for further information:  \n• https://sciences.ulb.be/en/computer-sciences (Computer Science Department) \n• http://mlg.ulb.ac.be (the ULB Machine Learning Group) \n \n \n \nWhere to go to apply? \nClick here:  https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2101/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nFor any connection problems or questions about our application, consult our FAQ : e-recrut-mode-d-\nemploi-candidat-en-_1734942996246-pdf \nN.B.: SAP complies with European and U.S. regulations and, as a result, does not allow access to its \napplication from the following countries/regions: Crimea, Sevastopol, the Donetsk People’s Republic (DNR) \n/ Luhansk People’s Republic (LNR), areas not controlled by the Ukrainian government in the Kherson and \nZaporizhzhia regions, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Russia, and Belarus.  \n \nTherefore, candidates applying from these countries – and only from these countries – can submit their CV \nand application to this address: rectrice@ulb.be \n \nEqual opportunities policy \nULB's personnel management policy is geared towards diversity and equal opportunities. \nWe recruit candidates on the basis of their skills, irrespective of age, gender, sexual orientation, origin, \nnationality, beliefs, disability, etc. \nWould you like to be provided with reasonable accommodation in the selection procedure because of a \ndisability, disorder, or illness?  Please contact Marie Botty, the person in charge of diversity aspects for the \nacademic and scientific staff (marie.botty@ulb.be). Be assured of the confidentiality of this information. \nMore details on the ULB gender and diversity policy are available at Diversity at ULB - ULB. \n \nYou will find all the regulations relating to academic careers on our site at \nhttp://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20507": {
      "title": "POSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PARTIEL (MINI-CHAIRE) EN DIDACTIQUE DES SCIENCES",
      "description": " \n  \n \n  \nSOUS RESERVE DE L’APPROBATION DU CONSEIL ACADEMIQUE DU 23 NOVEMBRE 2026 \n \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PARTIEL (MINI-CHAIRE) EN DIDACTIQUE DES \nSCIENCES \n(CORRESPONDANT A 40% DE TEMPS PLEIN, 30% ENSEIGNEMENT ET 10% RECHERCHE) \nFACULTE DES SCIENCES \n \nRéférence : 2027/A026 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures : 04/01/2027 à midi \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 14/09/2027 \nDescriptif du poste \nL’Université libre de Bruxelles ouvre un poste académique temporaire à temps partiel (0,4 d’un temps \nplein) pour dispenser des cours et animer des séances de travaux pratiques en collaboration avec les \nmembres de la Faculté des Sciences  actifs en didactique des sciences ou des mathématiques . Les \ndifférentes activités d’enseignement s’adressent à de futurs enseignants des sections S1, S2 et S3 et \nauront lieu sur des campus différents. Ils s’inscrivent dans le consortium constitué par l’ULB avec des \nHautes Écoles pédagogiques situées à Bruxelles et dans le Brabant wallon. \n \n Les activités d’apprentissage, qui pourraient être revues, incluent : \n• TRAN-F-9203 et TRAN-F-9205 « Ranger, trier, classer » (2 x 24 h théorie à Bruxelles et à Nivelles, \nsections 2 et 3, 2e année de bachelier) ; \n• TRAN-F-9300 « Energie » (24 h théorie à Bruxelles, section 3, 3e année de bachelier) ; \n• TRAN-F-9400 « Sciences et environnement » (24 h théorie à Bruxelles, section 1, 1e année de \nmaster) \nainsi que la coordination des travaux pratiques y afférents.  \n \nLe cours « Ranger, trier, classer » est adressé à de futur.e.s enseignant.e.s de l’école primaire (S2) et du \nsecondaire inférieur (S3), en deuxième année du bachelier. Le même cours de 24  h sera dispensé, en \nlangue française, 2 fois (à l’ULB et à Nivelles, sur le campus de la HE2B).  \nL’objectif du cours est de permettre aux futurs enseignants de développer des compétences liées aux \nsavoirs suivants :  \nBiologie : classification des vivants et travail du concept d’évolution.    \nPhysique : classification des éléments/phénomènes physiques, les états de la matière et les \nchangements d’état.   \nChimie : changements d’état, classification des éléments/phénomènes chimiques.     \nIl s’agit de mettre en lumière les différences de classifications dans ces trois branches, les critères positifs, \nnégatifs, observables ou non. \n \nLe cours « Energie » est adressé à de futur.e.s enseignant.e.s du secondaire inférieur (S3), en troisième \nannée du bachelier. Le cours de 24 h sera dispensé, en langue française, à l’ULB.  \nL’objectif du cours est de permettre aux futurs enseignants de développer des compétences liées aux \nsavoirs suivants : \n   \n \n \nTransformation, conservation et identification des différents types d’énergies.   \nBilans d’énergie.   \nÉnergie dans le vivant : le métabolisme, le cycle de l’énergie.   \nEnergie dans les réactions chimiques.   \nOrdre de grandeurs (en physique, biologie et chimie).   \nDurabilité, lien avec les ressources \n \nLe cours « Sciences et environnement » est adressé à de futur.e.s enseignant.e.s de l’école maternelle \n(S1), en première année du master. Le cours de 24 h sera dispensé, en langue française, à l’ULB.  \nL’objectif du cours est de permettre aux futurs enseignants de développer des compétences liées aux \nsavoirs suivants :  \n- Les enjeux de la durabilité dans la compréhension de l’environnement au niveau : \no de la matière et des ressources ;  \no des sources et des types d’énergie (y compris interprétations moléculaires ; \no du développement durable, de la pollution air-eau. \n \nLe/la candidat.e retenu.e sera nommé.e pour une durée initiale de 3 ans, renouvelable. Cet emploi est \nun emploi à temps partiel, à hauteur de 0,4 etp.  \n \nAu niveau de l’enseignement, le ou la titulaire sera de facto membre du Conseil de la Formation des \nEnseignants. Le ou la titulaire sera en outre invité.e à contribuer aux activités de recherche menées en \ndidactique des sciences au sein de la Faculté des sciences ; à ce titre, il ou elle pourra notamment \ndévelopper des collaborations avec les centres de recherche en développement au sein des hautes \nécoles ou écoles supérieures des arts partenaires.   \nTitre requis  \nDocteur à thèse en sciences (ou titre équivalent dans une université étrangère), ou titre jugé équivalent. \nCompétences et expériences requises \n• Vous avez des capacités à transmettre des savoirs dans le domaine des sciences et disposez d’une \nexpérience de recherche dans ce même domaine ; \n• Vous pouvez témoigner d’un intérêt pour les questions relatives à l’enseignement, la didactique des \nsciences, l’éducation et l’école, dans leurs liens avec les sciences ; \n• Vous avez une expérience de l’enseignement ; \n• Vous avez une excellente maîtrise de la langue française ; \n• Vous avez mené des recherches et publié des travaux sur des questions de didactique des sciences \nou de sciences ; \n• Vous avez une ancienneté de 4 années minimum au moment de l’engagement ; \n• Vous avez un sens de l'organisation et des responsabilités, une capacité d'adaptation et de flexibilité, \nune facilité de contact en enseignement, une autonomie et une capacité à travailler en équipe, un \nsens de l'initiative. \n \nIntéressé·e ? \nDes renseignements complémentaires peuvent être obtenus auprès du Prof. Cécile Moucheron (E-mail: \ncecile.moucheron@ulb.be ). \n   \n \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (si vous le souhaitez un CV type peut \nêtre téléchargé via le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-\net-scientifiques-cv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse \n(https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/2f-dossier-de-candidature-de-acad-tps-partiel-au-docx). \n \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants :  \n \n• Une lettre de motivation ;  \n• Un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les activités de recherche et un projet de \nrecherche, en ce compris l’insertion envisagée au sein des équipes de recherche de l’ULB ; \n• Un dossier d’enseignement comprenant un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les \nactivités d’enseignement antérieures et un projet d’enseignement pour les 5 premières années du \nmandat, qui s’intègre de manière cohérente dans la vision de l’entit é de rattachement et dans les \nprofils d’enseignements des filières de formation auxquelles le candidat devra contribuer ; \n• Les noms et adresses électroniques de contact de cinq personnes de référence susceptibles d’être \ncontactées par les organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des genres.   Ces \npersonnes ne peuvent être en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou affectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \n \nOù se rendre pour postuler ? \n \nCliquez ici : https://jobs.ulb.be/job-invite/2097/?isInternalUser=true  \n \nPour tout problème de connexion ou question à propos de notre application, consultez notre FAQ : e-\nrecrut-mode-d-emploi-candidat-fr-_1734942952302-pdf \n \nN.B. : SAP respecte des directives européennes et états-uniennes, et en conséquence, n’autorise pas \nles accès à son application à partir des pays/ régions suivants : La Crimée, Sébastopol, République \npopulaire de Donetsk (DNR) / République populaire de Louhansk (LNR), Les zones non contrôlées par le \ngouvernement ukrainien dans les oblasts de Kherson et Zaporijia, Cuba, l’Iran, La Corée du Nord, la \nSyrie, la Russie et la Biélorussie. \n \nDès lors, les candidats qui postulent au départ de ces pays – et uniquement au départ de ces pays – \npeuvent envoyer leur curriculum vitae et leur dossier de candidature à cette adresse : rectrice@ulb.be \n \nPolitique d’égalité des chances \nLa politique de gestion du personnel de l’ULB est axée sur la diversité et l’égalité des chances. \nNous recrutons les candidat·es en fonction de leurs compétences, indépendamment de leur âge, leur \ngenre, leur orientation sexuelle, leur origine, leur nationalité, leurs convictions, leur handicap, etc. \nVous souhaitez bénéficier d’aménagements raisonnables dans le cadre de la procédure de sélection en \nraison d’un handicap, d’un trouble ou d’une maladie ? N’hésitez pas à prendre contact avec Marie Botty \n(marie.botty@ulb.be) notre personne de contact en charge des aspects de diversité pour le personnel \nenseignant et scientifique. Soyez assuré·e de la confidentialité de cette information. \nPlus de détails sur les politiques de genre et de diversité sont disponibles sur https://www.ulb.be/fr/l-\nulb-s-engage/diversites.  \n   \n \n \nVous trouverez l’ensemble des dispositions relatives aux carrières du corps académique sur notre site à \nl’adresse http://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n \n \n "
    },
    "https://cwfront.ulb.ac.be/vacacad/vacancies/download/20636": {
      "title": "(CORRESPONDANT A 0,5/10 DE TEMPS PLEIN, SOIT UN FORFAIT HORAIRE DE 15H/AN) FACULTE DE MEDECINE",
      "description": " \n  \n \n \nPOSTE ACADEMIQUE TEMPS PARTIEL EN SCIENCES DENTAIRES \n(CORRESPONDANT A 0,5/10 DE TEMPS PLEIN, SOIT UN FORFAIT HORAIRE DE 15H/AN) \nFACULTE DE MEDECINE \n  \nRéférence : 2026/A092 \nDate limite du dépôt des candidatures :  27/11/2026 à midi  \nDate d’entrée en fonction prévue le : 01/01/2027 \n \nDescriptif du poste \nObjectifs pédagogiques et scientifiques :   \nA l'issue de cette Unité d'Enseignement, l'étudiant sera capable de maîtriser : \nAspects sociologiques : l'analyse et la compréhension des rapports entre facteurs comportementaux \net santé bucco-dentaire, la capacité à tenir compte de ces facteurs dans l'élaboration d'un plan de \ntraitement, l'aptitude à comprendre l'organisation des soins de santé et les facteurs qui les \ninfluencent, à comprendre les modes d'utilisation des mesures préventives dans les secteurs privé et \npublic, basés sur la littérature scientifique. \n \nCours repris dans la charge au moment du recrutement :  \n• DENT-G5519 – (30h Th) Odontologie médico-légale et aspects sociologiques - partim \nsociologie de la santé bucco-dentaire (15h Th) – Q2  \n• Contenu : \nAspects sociologiques : Notions d'épidémiologie et de statistique. Epidémiologie des \nmaladies bucco-dentaires, des maladies systémiques à répercussion bucco-dentaire en \nBelgique et ailleurs. Organisation des services de soins en Belgique et Union Européenne, \naspects de planification de l’offre de soins et la prise en charge des couts des soins. Base \nscientifique des mesures préventives collectifs et personnels en général et en Belgique. \nComparaison avec d'autres programmes de soins dentaires mis en pratique en Europe et \ndans le monde. \n• Cours obligatoire en bloc 5 \nTitre requis : \nTitulaire d’un Master en rapport avec la matière, titulaire d’une thèse de doctorat. \nCompétences requises : \n• Vous avez une expérience reconnue dans la discipline \n• Si vous ne parlez pas couramment la langue française (niveau C1), une période d’adaptation peut \nvous être accordée, mais vous devrez être capable d’enseigner en français à la fin de la troisième \nannée suivant votre nomination. \n \n \nIntéressé·e ? \nDes renseignements complémentaires peuvent être obtenus auprès Madame Astrid Vanden Abbeele, \nPrésidente de la Commission des Programmes Sciences dentaires (courriel : \nAstrid.Vanden.Abbeele@ulb.be). \nVotre dossier de candidature sera composé d’un Curriculum vitae (un CV type peut être téléchargeable \nvia le site internet : https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/emplois-academiques-et-scientifiques-\ncv-type ) et d’un document complété à l’aide du template disponible à cette adresse URL \n(https://www.ulb.be/fr/documents-officiels/3f-dossier-de-candidature-de-acad-tps-partiel-fh-docx).  \nCe canevas structure votre dossier de candidature en reprenant les éléments suivants : \n• une lettre de motivation  \n• un dossier d’enseignement comprenant un rapport de 7000 signes (ou 4 pages) environ sur les \nactivités d’enseignement antérieures et un projet d’enseignement pour les 5 premières années du \nmandat, qui s’intègre de manière cohérente dans la vision de l’entité de rattachement et dans les \nprofils d’enseignements des filières de formation auxquelles le candidat devra contribuer \n• les noms et adresses mail de contact de cinq personnes de référence susceptibles d’être \ncontactées par les organes chargés d’évaluer les dossiers, en veillant à l’équilibre des genres.  Ces \npersonnes ne peuvent être en conflit d’intérêt en raison de liens familiaux ou affectifs. \n \nLes dossiers incomplets ou les dossiers n'utilisant pas le canevas mis à votre disposition ne seront pas \nexaminés par la commission de sélection. \n \nOù se rendre pour postuler ? \nCliquez ici :  \nPour tout problème de connexion ou question à propos de notre application, consultez notre FAQ : e-\nrecrut-mode-d-emploi-candidat-fr-_1734942952302-pdf \nN.B. : SAP respecte des directives européennes et états-uniennes, et en conséquence, n’autorise pas \nles accès à son application à partir des pays/ régions suivants : La Crimée, Sébastopol, République \npopulaire de Donetsk (DNR) / République populaire de Louhansk (LNR), Les zones non contrôlées par \nle gouvernement ukrainien dans les oblasts de Kherson et Zaporijia, Cuba, l’Iran, La Corée du Nord, la \nSyrie, la Russie et la Biélorussie. \nDès lors, les candidats qui postulent au départ de ces pays – et uniquement au départ de ces pays – \npeuvent envoyer leur curriculum vitae et leur dossier de candidature à cette adresse : rectrice@ulb.be \n \nPolitique d’égalité des chances \nLa politique de gestion du personnel de l’ULB est axée sur la diversité et l’égalité des chances. \nNous recrutons les candidat·es en fonction de leurs compétences, indépendamment de leur âge, leur \ngenre, leur orientation sexuelle, leur origine, leur nationalité, leurs convictions, leur handicap, etc. \nVous souhaitez bénéficier d’aménagements raisonnables dans le cadre de la procédure de sélection en \nraison d’un handicap, d’un trouble ou d’une maladie ? N’hésitez pas à prendre contact avec Marie \nBotty, (marie.botty@ulb.be), notre personne de contact en charge des aspects de diversité pour le \npersonnel enseignant et scientifique.  Soyez assuré·e de la confidentialité de cette information.\n \n   \n \n \nPlus de détails sur les politiques de genre et de diversité sont disponibles sur https://www.ulb.be/fr/l-\nulb-s-engage/diversites.  \n \nVous trouverez l’ensemble des dispositions relatives aux carrières du corps académique sur notre site \nà l’adresse http://www.ulb.ac.be/emploi/academique.html. \n "
